B.amP=new A.aN("app-notifications",B.bmb,B.aZF,'The app has two kinds of reminders, and you control each one yourself:\n- Prayer alerts: open Prayer Times. Each prayer has a bell next to it. Tap the bell to switch that prayer\'s alert on or off (when it is on the bell reads "Turn off the Fajr alert", for example). Lower on the same screen, the Phone notifications card has "Also remind me before", where you pick No or a number of minutes. On the Android and iPhone apps the notification arrives even when the app is closed; in a web browser, alerts only work while the page is open.\n- Zakat reminders: each one has its own switch on the Zakat screen.\n\nTo stop notifications from the phone itself, use your phone\'s settings: Apps, then Ar-Rayaan, then Notifications. Nothing in this app sends a notification you have not switched on.\n[GO:/prayer]\n[GO:/zakat]',"notifications",!0,"")
B.aS2=s(["\\b(?:dua|supplication)s?\\b.*\\b(?:toilet|bathroom|lavatory|restroom|washroom|latrine|call of nature|relieving)\\b","\\b(?:toilet|bathroom|lavatory|restroom|washroom|latrine)\\b.*\\b(?:dua|supplication)s?\\b","\\bwhat (?:do i|should i|to|do we|should we|is it that i should) (?:say|recite|read)\\b.*\\b(?:enter\\w*|leav\\w*|exit\\w*|go\\w* (?:in|to|into)|us\\w*|coming out)\\b.*\\b(?:toilet|bathroom|lavatory|restroom|washroom|latrine)\\b","\\bghufranak\\b","\\bkhubuth\\b","\\bdua (?:for )?(?:entering|leaving|exiting) (?:the )?(?:khala|toilet)\\b"],t.s)
B.amT=new A.aN("dua-toilet",B.aS2,B.b,'On entering the toilet, the Prophet \ufdfa used to say (Sahih al-Bukhari 142):\n\n\u0627\u0644\u0644\u0651\u064e\u0647\u064f\u0645\u0651\u064e \u0625\u0650\u0646\u0651\u0650\u064a \u0623\u064e\u0639\u064f\u0648\u0630\u064f \u0628\u0650\u0643\u064e \u0645\u0650\u0646\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0652\u062e\u064f\u0628\u064f\u062b\u0650 \u0648\u064e\u0627\u0644\u0652\u062e\u064e\u0628\u064e\u0627\u0626\u0650\u062b\u0650\n\nAllahumma inni a\'udhu bika minal-khubuthi wal-khaba\'ith.\nMeaning: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils (and from filth and evil).\n\nOn coming out, he used to say (Sunan Abu Dawud 30, sahih per al-Albani):\n\n\u063a\u064f\u0641\u0652\u0631\u064e\u0627\u0646\u064e\u0643\u064e\n\nGhufranaka. Meaning: I ask You for Your forgiveness.\n\nSay the first before you go in (or before uncovering yourself, if you are outdoors), and the second when you come out. Many people begin with "Bismillah" first, and enter with the left foot and leave with the right; scholars differ on how firm the report for "Bismillah" is, and the du\'a above is the part in Sahih al-Bukhari. These are said silently, in the heart or under the breath, not aloud inside the toilet. The rest of the manners are in the istinja answer: ask me "toilet etiquette".\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 142; Sunan Abu Dawud 30, sahih per al-Albani.',"toilet",!0,"")
B.aQm=s(["\\b(?:losing|lost|lose|loosing) (?:my |the )?(?:faith|iman|belief|religion|deen)\\b","\\bmy (?:faith|iman|belief) (?:is|has|feels|got|was) (?:weak|weaker|gone|slipping|fading|dying|shaky|shaken|dead|low)\\b","\\bi (?:have|am having|keep having|got|ve got|feel) (?:some |many |a lot of |lots of )?doubts?\\b","\\bdoubts? (?:about|in|on|regarding) (?:islam|my faith|my religion|allah|god|the quran|the prophet|religion|everything)\\b","\\b(?:struggling|struggle|struggles) (?:with|in) (?:my )?(?:faith|iman|belief|believing)\\b","\\bi (?:am not|m not|am no longer|dont feel|do not feel|dont know if i am|do not know if i am) (?:sure|certain|convinced) (?:i |that i )?(?:believe|still believe|have faith)\\b","\\bi (?:dont|do not|cant|cannot|cant) (?:really )?(?:feel|find|have) (?:any |the |my )?(?:faith|iman|belief|connection to (?:allah|god))\\b","\\bquestioning (?:my |the )?(?:faith|islam|religion|iman|belief|everything)\\b","\\bi (?:dont|do not) know (?:if|whether|what) (?:i )?(?:believe|to believe)\\b","\\bwhat if (?:islam|it all|religion|everything) (?:is|isnt|is not) (?:true|real|false|wrong)\\b"],t.s)
B.b6C=s(["\\b(?:increase|strengthen|boost|build|improve|renew|refresh|restore)\\b","\\b(?:leave|leaving|quit|quitting|abandon|renounce|exit)\\b"],t.s)
B.an8=new A.aN("faith-doubt",B.aQm,B.b6C,'Thank you for telling me this. It is not easy to say, and I will not rush to fix you or lecture you.\n\nDoubt is more common than people admit, and it is not the same as having left. Some of the Companions came to the Prophet \ufdfa troubled by thoughts they felt were too terrible to say out loud. He did not shame them (Sahih Muslim 132). Ibrahim \ufdfa asked Allah to show him how He gives life to the dead; when Allah asked "Have you not believed?" he said "Yes, but [I ask] only that my heart may be satisfied" (Qur\'an 2:260). Wanting the heart settled is not the same as denying.\n\nSome things that often help:\n- Say what the doubt is actually about. Is it a question (why is there suffering, how do I know the Qur\'an is preserved, how do I know there is a God)? Is prayer feeling empty? Did someone in the community hurt you? Each needs a different answer. Tell me in your own words and I will answer from the sources where I can, and say plainly where I cannot.\n- Do not carry it alone. A trusted teacher or imam who can listen without panicking, or a friend, is worth finding. A scholar can answer what I cannot.\n- Keep the small things you can: a short prayer, a few ayat, a single honest sentence to Allah. Faith rises and falls; it is not always at the same height. Allah says: "And when My servants ask you, [O Muhammad], concerning Me - indeed I am near" (Qur\'an 2:186).\n- If this comes with heaviness, hopelessness or thoughts of harming yourself, please tell me, and I will take that first. "Need help now" opens help lines for your country.\n\nI am an app, not a person or a scholar, and I cannot see your heart. What I can do is stay with the question with you.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 132; Qur\'an 2:260, 2:186.\n[GO:/academy/aqeedah]\n[GO:/feelings]',"faith",!0,"")
B.bm1=s(["\\bapostas\\w*\\b","\\bapostates?\\b","\\bmurtad\\w*\\b","\\briddah\\b","\\bridda\\b","\\b(?:leaving|leave|leaves|left|quit|quitting|abandon\\w*|renounc\\w*|exit\\w*) (?:from )?(?:the )?(?:islam|religion of islam)\\b.*\\b(?:punish\\w*|death|kill\\w*|penalty|penalties|ruling|rulings|law|laws|sin|allowed|permitted|haram|consequences?|crime|executed|execution|hell|fire)\\b","\\b(?:punish\\w*|death|kill\\w*|penalty|penalties|ruling|rulings|law|laws|sin|allowed|permitted|haram|consequences?|crime|executed|execution)\\b.*\\b(?:leaving|leave|leaves|left|quit|quitting|abandon\\w*|renounc\\w*) (?:from )?(?:the )?islam\\b","\\bwhat happens (?:if|when) (?:a )?(?:muslim|someone|you|i|one|people) (?:leave|leaves|left|quit|quits|abandons?) islam\\b","\\bcan (?:a )?(?:muslim|someone|you) (?:leave|quit|abandon) islam\\b","\\bfreedom of (?:religion|belief|faith|conscience)\\b","\\bcompulsion in religion\\b","\\bis it (?:true|a fact) that (?:muslims|ex muslims|people who leave islam)\\b.*\\b(?:killed|executed|die|death)\\b","\\bex muslims?\\b"],t.s)
