B.alu=new A.aN("apostasy-ruling",B.bm1,B.aVK,'This is one of the most argued-over questions about Islam, so here is a straight answer with the texts and the disagreement, not a dodge.\n\nWhat the texts say:\n- The Qur\'an protects freedom of belief: "There shall be no compulsion in [acceptance of] the religion" (Qur\'an 2:256), and "whoever wills - let him believe; and whoever wills - let him disbelieve" (Qur\'an 18:29). It warns of the loss in the Hereafter for one who turns back and dies in disbelief (Qur\'an 2:217). It does not name a punishment for this in the world.\n- Hadith: Ibn Abbas reported that the Prophet said if somebody discards his religion, kill him (Sahih al-Bukhari 3017), and Abdullah reported the Prophet said the blood of a Muslim who confesses that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah cannot be shed except in three cases: a life for a life, a married person who commits illegal sexual intercourse, and the one who leaves Islam and separates from the community (Sahih al-Bukhari 6878).\n\nHow scholars have read them:\n- The majority of classical jurists held that someone who openly leaves Islam is first called to repent, and that if he does not, a court may punish it with death. The schools differ on details, such as the time given to repent and whether a woman is treated the same (the Hanafi school does not put a woman to death for it).\n- Other scholars, early and today, read the reports as a penalty for treason, deserting to an enemy or fighting the community (note the words "and separates from the community"), not for a private change of belief. They point to the verses above, and to the bedouin who asked the Prophet to cancel his pledge to Islam and left Madinah: he refused to cancel it, but did not punish him (Sahih al-Bukhari 7211).\n- On one point there is wide agreement: this belongs to a lawful court, never to a family, a neighbour or a crowd. A person who hurts someone for leaving Islam is acting against Islam, and breaks the law in most countries.\n\nI do not give a legal ruling, and this is not a verdict. A qualified scholar can tell you the position of a school in detail.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 2:256, 18:29, 2:217; Sahih al-Bukhari 3017, 6878, 7211.\n[GO:/sources]',"apostasy",!0,"")
B.b9n=s(["\\b(?:thinking (?:of|about)|want(?:ed)? to|going to|wanna|planning to|considering|should i|about to|ready to|i want out and)\\s+(?:be\\s+)?(?:leave|leaving|quit|quitting|abandon\\w*|renounc\\w*|exit\\w*|stop being)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|muslim|religion|faith|deen)\\b","\\bwhat do you think (?:about|of) (?:me )?(?:leaving|quitting|abandoning|renouncing)\\b.*\\b(?:islam|religion|faith)\\b","\\bi (?:dont|do not|no longer|cant|cannot) want to be (?:a )?muslim( anymore| any more| now)?\\b","\\bi (?:left|have left|am leaving|am done with|quit|have quit|am quitting|gave up) (?:on )?(?:islam|the religion|my religion|being muslim|my faith)\\b","\\bi (?:no longer|dont|do not|stopped|stop) believ\\w* (?:in )?(?:islam|allah|god|the quran|religion)\\b","\\bi (?:want|wish) (?:to )?(?:leave|get out of|be out of) islam\\b","\\bi am (?:an? )?(?:ex muslim|exmuslim|atheist|agnostic|apostate)\\b","\\bi (?:became|have become|am becoming) (?:an? )?(?:atheist|agnostic|ex muslim)\\b","\\bi (?:hate|am sick of|am tired of|cant stand) (?:being (?:a )?muslim|islam|my religion)\\b"],t.s)
