B.al4=new A.aN("leaving-islam-personal",B.b9n,B.bja,"I am glad you told me, and did not just go quiet with it. I will be honest with you: I will not pretend to be neutral about what Islam teaches, and I will not pressure you either.\n\nWhat the Qur'an says first is that belief cannot be forced: \"There shall be no compulsion in [acceptance of] the religion\" (Qur'an 2:256). No person, family or app is meant to frighten you into faith. Muslims also believe that turning away from the truth is serious before Allah (Qur'an 3:85), and I would not be honest if I hid that. But the judgment on any heart belongs to Allah, not to me and not to anyone around you.\n\nWhat I would rather do is hear what is behind it. People step away for very different reasons: honest questions nobody answered well, being hurt by Muslims or by a harsh family or community, grief, a faith that went numb, a new life or relationship, or simply not believing. Those are not the same, and I would speak differently to each. If you want to tell me, I will listen and answer from the sources where I can, and say so where I cannot.\n\nA few things that may matter right now:\n- You do not have to decide today, or alone. A teacher or imam who listens without shouting, or a friend, is worth talking to, and so is anyone you trust outside Islam.\n- If you are afraid of how your family or community would react, your safety comes first. \"Need help now\" opens help lines for your country. By default, what you type to me stays on your device.\n- Whatever you decide, you are still a person with dignity. No private individual has the right to harm or punish you for it.\n\nTell me what is behind it, if you like, and I will start there.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:256, 3:85.\n[GO:/academy/aqeedah]\n[GO:/feelings]","faith",!0,"")
B.b_8=s(["\\b9 ?:? ?5\\b","\\b(?:surah |sura )?(?:at )?(?:tawbah|taubah|tawba|bara.?ah|baraat)\\b.*\\b(?:5|five|kill|sword|polytheists|idolaters)\\b","\\bsword verses?\\b","\\bayat? (?:as )?sayf\\b","\\bkill (?:the )?(?:polytheists|idolaters|mushrikin|mushrikeen|pagans|disbelievers|unbelievers|infidels|kafirs?|non muslims?)\\b","\\b(?:quran|koran|islam|muslims?)\\b.*\\b(?:say|says|tell|tells|command|commands|order|orders|teach|teaches|allow|allows)\\b.*\\bkill\\b.*\\b(?:non muslims?|disbelievers|infidels|kafirs?|unbelievers|polytheists|idolaters|pagans|christians|jews)\\b","\\bfight (?:them|the polytheists|the disbelievers) wherever you find\\b","\\bwherever you find them\\b"],t.s)
B.an5=new A.aN("nine-five-sword",B.b_8,B.b,'Surah at-Tawbah 9:5 is often quoted on its own. Read in order, it belongs to a passage about a specific war: the idolaters of Makkah who had broken their treaties with the Muslims.\n\n- The passage opens by ending the treaties with those idolaters who had broken them (Qur\'an 9:1). In the same breath it protects those who had not: "Excepted are those with whom you made a treaty among the polytheists and then they have not been deficient toward you in anything or supported anyone against you; so complete for them their treaty until their term [has ended]" (Qur\'an 9:4).\n- Verse 5 then says: "And when the sacred months have passed, then kill the polytheists wherever you find them and capture them and besiege them and sit in wait for them at every place of ambush. But if they should repent, establish prayer, and give zakah, let them [go] on their way" (Qur\'an 9:5).\n- The very next verse commands protection, not killing: "And if any one of the polytheists seeks your protection, then grant him protection so that he may hear the words of Allah. Then deliver him to his place of safety" (Qur\'an 9:6).\n- And the reason is given a few verses on: "Would you not fight a people who broke their oaths and determined to expel the Messenger, and they had begun [the attack upon] you the first time" (Qur\'an 9:13).\n\nHow scholars read it: most take it as addressed to those particular hostile idolaters, at that time and in a state of war, and not as a standing order to kill anyone for not being Muslim. The same book says "Allah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion and do not expel you from your homes - from being righteous toward them and acting justly toward them" (Qur\'an 60:8), and the Prophet \ufdfa warned: Abdullah ibn Amr reported the Prophet said whoever killed a person having a treaty with the Muslims shall not smell the smell of Paradise (Sahih al-Bukhari 3166). Some classical commentators did say this verse cancelled the gentler verses on tolerance (the "sword verse" idea); many scholars, early and modern, reject that and keep 9:5 tied to its context of war. Scholars differ, and I am not the one to settle it.\n\nIf you want the wider teaching on fighting and peace, ask me "what is jihad?". For a ruling, ask a qualified scholar.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 9:1, 9:4, 9:5, 9:6, 9:13, 60:8; Sahih al-Bukhari 3166.\n[GO:/quran]',"peace",!0,"")
