B.als=new A.aN("app-maker-tradition",B.aQX,B.b,"Two questions, answered plainly.\n\nWho made it: Ar-Rayaan is an app of RHW Technologies, and the owner is Abdul G Khokhar. That is what the app states. It gives no funder, address or company details on any screen I can read from, so I have none to give you, and I will not guess any. What it does say: the Terms of Service (in Settings) describe Ar-Rayaan as a study and reflection companion, not a religious authority, and Our Sources says no named scholar has reviewed the app yet.\n\nSunni or Shia: I answer from the Sunni tradition, from the Qur'an and the Sunnah as the Sunni scholars transmit them, and where schools of law differ I name the Hanafi, Maliki, Shafi'i and Hanbali views. The hadith collections the app cites are the six main Sunni books (Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, and the four Sunan). It does not teach Shia law, and it does not rank or attack any Muslim group; where a question divides Sunni and Shia I say so rather than choose for you. Ask me \"what is the difference between Sunni and Shia?\" for the neutral account.\n\nOn cost: everything in this app, including me, is free today, and nothing asks for a card.\n[GO:/sources]\n[GO:/settings]","about hadi",!0,"")
B.b4F=s(["\\b(?:be|become) my (?:friend|companion|buddy|bestie|mate|best friend)\\b","\\b(?:are|r) you my (?:friend|companion|buddy)\\b","\\bcan (?:we|you and i) be (?:friends|best friends|buddies)\\b","\\bi (?:want|need) (?:a |you as a )?(?:friend|someone to talk to|somebody to talk to)\\b","\\bi have no (?:friends?|one to talk to|body to talk to)\\b","\\b(?:will|would) you be my friend\\b","\\bdo you (?:like|love|care about|miss) me\\b","\\bcan i (?:talk|vent) to you\\b","\\bcan we (?:just )?(?:talk|chat)\\b"],t.s)
B.alm=new A.aN("companion-friend",B.b4F,B.b,"I would like to be useful to you, and I will be honest about what I am: an app. I am not a person. I do not remember you the way a friend does, I cannot sit with you in a hard hour, and I will not notice if you go quiet. A friend should be a real person, and I do not want to stand in the place of one.\n\nWhat I can do is talk about Islam and about this app, give you a du'a or a story, think a question through with you, and listen to what is on your mind. You are welcome to do that here, any time.\n\nFor the rest, real people: a relative or an old friend you have lost touch with; someone at your local masjid, or a class or halaqah there; a neighbour or colleague; and in a hard season, an imam or counsellor you can see in person. The Prophet \ufdfa said Abu Hurairah reported the Prophet said a man is upon the religion of his friend, so let one of you look at whom he befriends (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2378, hasan per al-Albani). I would like you to have good ones.\n\nIf you are feeling very alone or low, tell me, and I will stay with that. \"Need help now\" opens help lines for your country.\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2378, hasan per al-Albani.\n[GO:/feelings]\n[GO:/search]","about hadi",!0,"")
B.aUl=s(["^(?:im |i am |i m )?(?:so |really |very |just )?bored$","\\b(?:im|i am|i m|i feel) (?:so |really |very |just )?bored\\b","\\bentertain me\\b"],t.s)
B.ann=new A.aN("bored",B.aUl,B.b,"Let us fix that. A few ideas:\n- A story: the Stories section has the prophets, the companions, the Prophet's life and short tales, each with its sources.\n- A game: Games has Qur'an knowledge, Stories trivia, the 99 Names, a word search, Ludo and chess. They keep no points, coins or ranks.\n- A question: something you have always wondered about Islam. Ask me, and I will answer from the sources or say plainly that I cannot.\n- Something small that is good for you: a short du'a, or a few ayat read slowly.\n\nI am an app, so I cannot play or chat like a friend, but I am glad to help you find something worth your time.\n[GO:/stories]\n[GO:/games]","about hadi",!0,"")
B.b72=s(["\\bevolution\\b","\\bevolve\\w*\\b","\\bdarwin\\w*\\b","\\bnatural selection\\b","\\b(?:did|do|were) (?:humans?|we|men|people|adam) (?:come|descend|evolve|created)\\w* (?:from|out of) (?:apes?|monkeys?|animals?|primates?)\\b","\\bhuman origins?\\b.*\\b(?:science|islam)\\b"],t.s)
B.ama=new A.aN("evolution",B.b72,B.b,"Short, honest answer: Muslims do not all agree on this, and it is a question for a scholar who also understands the science. I do not have a scholar-reviewed position to give you.\n\nWhat nearly all scholars agree on: Allah is the Creator of everything, and the Qur'an teaches that Adam was created by Allah from clay and given a soul breathed from Him, and that the angels were told to prostrate to him (\"Indeed, I am going to create a human being from clay. So when I have proportioned him and breathed into him of My [created] soul, then fall down to him in prostration\" (Qur'an 38:71-72)). It also says: \"Indeed, the example of Jesus to Allah is like that of Adam. He created Him from dust\" (Qur'an 3:59).\n\nWhere views divide:\n- Many scholars, early and recent, say Adam was created directly and was not descended from earlier creatures, so they reject the evolution of human beings, while some accept change over time in other living things.\n- Some contemporary Muslim scholars and scientists accept that the sciences describe how life developed, and read the Qur'an's account of Adam as a special act of Allah within that history.\n- Others reject evolutionary theory as a whole, on religious or on scientific grounds.\n\nI will not pick one for you. If it worries your belief, that is a fair question: ask a qualified scholar, ideally one who has studied the science, and keep asking.\n\nSource: Qur'an 38:71-72, 3:59.\n[GO:/academy/aqeedah]","evolution",!0,"")
