B.amX=new A.aN("fatiha-in-prayer",B.blK,B.bmL,"Yes. Reciting al-Fatihah (the opening chapter of the Qur'an) is part of every rak'ah, and the Prophet \ufdfa said: whoever does not recite al-Fatihah in his prayer, his prayer is invalid (Sahih al-Bukhari 756) (Sahih Muslim 394).\n\nThe schools differ on the detail. The Shafi'i, Maliki and Hanbali schools make al-Fatihah a pillar in every rak'ah. The Hanafi school makes the Fatihah wajib in every rak'ah of the obligatory prayers (leaving it on purpose is sinful and you repeat the prayer) and says some recitation of the Qur'an in the first two rak'ahs fulfils the pillar. After the Fatihah, in the first two rak'ahs, you add another surah or a few verses. In the last rak'ah of a three- or four-rak'ah prayer, al-Fatihah alone is enough.\n\nBehind an imam: the schools differ on whether you recite the Fatihah behind him in the loud prayers; follow your school.\n\nIf you do not yet know it by heart, say the words as best you can and keep learning. A man who could not memorise any Qur'an asked the Prophet \ufdfa for something that would be enough; he told him to say \"Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is most great, and there is no might and no strength but in Allah\" (Sunan Abu Dawud 832, hasan per Darussalam).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 756; Sahih Muslim 394; Sunan Abu Dawud 832, hasan per Darussalam.\n[GO:/quran]","fatiha",!0,"")
B.aIa=s(["\\btashahhud\\b","\\bat ?tahiyyat\\b","\\btahiyyat\\b","\\blast sitting\\b","\\bfinal sitting\\b","\\bwhat (?:do i|should i|to) (?:say|recite|read) (?:when|in|during) (?:the )?(?:sitting|jalsa|qaada)\\b","\\bsalawat\\b","\\bdurood\\b","\\bdarood\\b","\\bsalat ?\\w* ibrahim\\b","\\bibrahimiyya\\b","\\bsend(?:ing)? blessings? on the prophet\\b","\\bwhat (?:do i|should i) say after tashahhud\\b"],t.s)
