B.amE=new A.aN("zakat-installments",B.bfm,B.aR1,"Paying in parts depends on whether it is before the due date or after it.\n\nBefore it is due, yes. It is reported that Al-Abbas asked the Prophet \ufdfa about paying his zakat early, before the year was complete, and that he allowed it (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 678, da'if per Darussalam). Al-Albani and Ahmad Shakir graded this report hasan, so the graders differ, and most scholars accept the early payment. So you may set an amount aside each month and give it as zakat, saying in your heart that it is your zakat when you give it. On your zakat date, work out the full amount. If what you gave is less, give the rest then. If it is more, ask a scholar whether the extra may count towards next year. The schools differ on how far ahead you may pay, so a scholar of your school should confirm.\n\nAfter it is due, no: once the year has passed, zakat is owed, and most scholars say it should be paid promptly. Delaying it without a reason is wrong, and unpaid zakat stays owed. If you cannot pay it all at once, for example because your money is tied up, pay what you can now and the rest as soon as you can, and ask a scholar who knows your case what is allowed.\n\nThe Zakat calculator keeps your numbers on your device and works out the full amount for your date.\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 678, da'if per Darussalam.\n[GO:/zakat]\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-zakat]","zakat",!0,"")
B.bnG=s(["\\bzakat\\b.*\\b\\d{2,}\\b","\\b\\d{2,}\\b.*\\bzakat\\b"],t.s)
B.bcW=s(["\\b(?:fitr|fitra|fitrana|recipients?)\\b","\\b(?:grams?|gms?|tola|carat|karat|jewel\\w*|gold|silver|hajj|umrah|days?|years?|months?|rakahs?|ayah|surah|verse|hadith|chapter|page|lesson)\\b","\\bpay (?:it )?in (?:instal?lments?|parts)\\b","\\b(?:mortgage\\w*|loans?|credit cards?|debts?)\\b"],t.s)
B.akO=new A.aN("zakat-sum",B.bnG,B.bcW,"To find your zakat, take 2.5% of the zakatable wealth you hold on your zakat date, which is the same as dividing it by 40. That is your figure only when three things are true:\n- It is at or above the nisab: the value of 85 grams of gold or 595 grams of silver in your own currency. The Prophet \ufdfa set the silver measure at five awqiyah (Sahih al-Bukhari 1447). The Zakat calculator can fill in today's gold and silver prices.\n- It has stayed at or above the nisab for one full lunar year (the hawl).\n- It is wealth that is yours to use: savings, cash, gold and silver, and goods you hold to sell count. The home you live in and the things you use every day do not.\n\nDebts that are due now may be taken off first, depending on your school; ask me \"what about debts\". Money you spent before the year ended is not counted.\n\nFor your exact figure with today's prices, open the Zakat calculator. It keeps your numbers on your device.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1447.\n[GO:/zakat]\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-zakat]","zakat",!0,"")
B.blL=s(["\\bwhen (?:is|does|do|should|must|will|did|are)\\b.*\\bzakat\\b.*\\b(?:due|payable|pay|paid|obligatory|required|owed|fall|falls|start|starts|begin|begins|become|becomes|calculated)\\b","\\bwhen (?:to|do i|should i|must i|can i|shall i) (?:pay|give|calculate|work out) (?:my |the )?zakat\\b","\\bzakat\\b.*\\b(?:due date|deadline|hawl|lunar year|one year|a year|yearly|annual\\w*|every year|each year|what date|which day|which month)\\b","\\bhawl\\b","\\bwhen is it (?:due|payable)\\b.*\\bzakat\\b"],t.s)
B.aMd=s(["\\b(?:fitr|fitra|recipients?)\\b"],t.s)
B.akW=new A.aN("zakat-due",B.blL,B.aMd,"Zakat falls due when your zakatable wealth has stayed at or above the nisab for one full lunar year (the hawl). The one-year condition is taught by all four schools, and it rests on reports such as Sunan Abu Dawud 1573, da'if per Darussalam. Al-Albani graded the same report sahih, so the graders differ. That is why I give you the rule the schools agree on and not one proof.\n\nHow to find your date:\n- Your zakat date is the day your wealth first reached the nisab. A year later, if you still hold at least the nisab, pay 2.5% of what you hold that day.\n- A lunar year is about 354 days, so the date moves about 11 days earlier in the calendar each year.\n- Many people choose one fixed day every year, such as the 1st of Ramadan, to keep it simple, and work out their zakat on that day. If you do, use the same day each year. Ask a scholar if you are changing your date.\n- If your wealth drops below the nisab part-way through the year, the schools differ: the Hanafi school looks at the two ends of the year, and the other schools restart the count when it falls below.\n- Pay it soon after it falls due. Unpaid zakat does not disappear with time; it stays owed.\n- Crops are different: their zakat is due at the harvest (\"give its due [zakah] on the day of its harvest\" (Qur'an 6:141)).\n\nZakat al-fitr is a separate charity at the end of Ramadan; ask me about it by name. The Zakat screen works out the amount once you know your date.\n\nSource: Sunan Abu Dawud 1573, da'if per Darussalam; Qur'an 6:141.\n[GO:/zakat]\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-zakat]","zakat",!0,"")
B.b2p=s(["\\bzakat\\b.*\\b(?:debts?|loans?|owe money|owed money|money i owe|i owe (?:people|someone|the bank|a lot)|owing money|mortgage\\w*|credit cards?|liabilit\\w*|borrow\\w*|in debt|arrears|bills)\\b","\\b(?:debts?|loans?|owe money|owed money|money i owe|i owe (?:people|someone|the bank|a lot)|owing money|mortgage\\w*|credit cards?|liabilit\\w*|in debt)\\b.*\\bzakat\\b"],t.s)
B.bnm=s(["\\b(?:recipients?|who can receive|who gets|eligib\\w*)\\b"],t.s)
B.alz=new A.aN("zakat-debts",B.b2p,B.bnm,"Debts you owe can reduce the wealth you pay zakat on, but only debts that are due now, and the schools differ:\n- The Hanafi, Maliki and Hanbali schools take the debts you owe away from your cash and gold before they work out whether you have reached the nisab and what you pay on. Zakat is paid on what is left.\n- The Shafi'i school's usual position is that debts do not reduce it: the full amount you hold is counted. The Zakat screen lets you choose, and shows the working for both.\n- Contemporary scholars often count only the instalments that are due within the year for a long loan such as a mortgage, not the whole loan. Ask a scholar if you have one.\n- Money other people owe you and that you can collect counts as your wealth. Money you cannot expect to get back does not, until you have it.\n- A debt does not cancel zakat if you are still over the nisab after taking it off. Repaying a debt that is due is also a duty, so do both.\n\nAllah names \"those in debt\" among the people who may receive zakat (Qur'an 9:60). If your debts are heavy, you may be one of them.\n\nThis is general guidance. For an exact figure with a business, a pension or a mortgage, ask a qualified scholar.\n\nSource: Qur'an 9:60.\n[GO:/zakat]\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-zakat]","zakat",!0,"")
B.bl9=s(["\\bnisab\\b","\\bhow (?:much|many)\\b.*\\bzakat\\b","\\bzakat\\b.*\\bhow (?:much|many)\\b","\\bzakat (?:rate|amount|percentage|percent|share)\\b","\\b(?:2.5|two and a half)\\b.*\\b(?:zakat|percent|%)\\b","\\b(?:zakat|percent|%)\\b.*\\b(?:2.5|two and a half)\\b","\\bwhat (?:percent|percentage|fraction|part) .*\\bzakat\\b","\\bzakat\\b.*\\bwhat (?:percent|percentage|fraction)\\b"],t.s)
