B.amg=new A.aN("kaaba",B.boF,B.b4s,"The Ka'bah is the cube-shaped House of Allah in the middle of the Sacred Mosque in Makkah. It is the direction (qiblah) that Muslims face in prayer: \"So turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Haram. And wherever you [believers] are, turn your faces toward it [in prayer]\" (Qur'an 2:144).\n\nAllah says it was the first house of worship for mankind: \"Indeed, the first House [of worship] established for mankind was that at Makkah - blessed and a guidance for the worlds\" (Qur'an 3:96). It was raised by Ibrahim and his son Ismail: \"And [mention] when Abraham was raising the foundations of the House and [with him] Ishmael\" (Qur'an 2:127). Pilgrims circle it in the rite of tawaf during Hajj and Umrah, and Hajj to it is a duty for those who are able (Qur'an 3:97).\n\nMuslims do not worship the Ka'bah or the Black Stone set in its corner; they worship Allah alone. The Ka'bah is a sign of unity: all Muslims in the world pray in its direction. The Qibla screen in this app shows the direction from where you are.\n\nSource: Qur'an 2:144, 3:96, 2:127, 3:97.\n[GO:/qibla]","kaaba",!0,"")
B.b1g=s(["\\bwho is (?:allah|god)\\b","\\bwhat is allah\\b","\\bwho is the god of (?:islam|muslims)\\b","\\bwho do muslims worship\\b","\\bis allah (?:a different god|god|the same as god)\\b","\\bwhat do muslims believe about (?:allah|god)\\b","\\bdescribe allah\\b","\\bwhat is tawheed\\b","\\bwhat is tawhid\\b","\\bwhat is shirk\\b","\\bwhat does allah mean\\b","\\bwhere is allah\\b","\\bdoes allah exist\\b","\\bprove (?:that )?(?:allah|god)\\b","\\bhow many gods\\b","\\bis there only one god\\b","\\bis allah real\\b"],t.s)
B.bjf=s(["\\b(?:99|ninety nine|names game|names of allah game|game)\\b"],t.s)
B.am7=new A.aN("who-is-allah",B.b1g,B.bjf,'Allah is the Arabic name of the One God, Creator and Lord of everything, the same God worshipped by Ibrahim, Musa and Isa. The Qur\'an gives the simplest description in Surah Al-Ikhlas: "He is Allah, [who is] One" (Qur\'an 112:1), "Allah, the Eternal Refuge" (Qur\'an 112:2), "He neither begets nor is born" (Qur\'an 112:3), "Nor is there to Him any equivalent" (Qur\'an 112:4).\n\nSome of what He tells us about Himself:\n- "There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the Hearing, the Seeing" (Qur\'an 42:11): nothing in creation resembles Him.\n- "He is Allah, other than whom there is no deity, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed. He is the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful" (Qur\'an 59:22).\n- "Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of [all] existence. Neither drowsiness overtakes Him nor sleep." (Qur\'an 2:255)\n\nThis oneness (tawhid) is the heart of Islam. Worshipping anything with Him is shirk: "Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills" (Qur\'an 4:48). Muslims know Him through His Names; the 99 Names game and screen in this app teach them.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 112:1, 112:2, 112:3, 112:4, 42:11, 59:22, 2:255, 4:48.\n[GO:/games/names99]',"allah",!0,"")
B.bl4=s(["\\bjibreel\\b","\\bjibril\\b","\\bgabriel\\b","\\bmikail\\b","\\bmichael\\b.*\\b(?:angel|islam)\\b","\\bwho (?:are|were) (?:the )?angels\\b","\\bwhat are angels\\b","\\bangels? (?:in|of) islam\\b","\\bwhat do muslims believe about angels\\b","\\bare angels (?:male|female|real)\\b","\\bwhat are angels made of\\b","\\bwho is the angel of death\\b","\\bmalik al mawt\\b","\\bazrail\\b","\\bazrael\\b","\\bisrafil\\b","\\bkiraman katibin\\b","\\bguardian angels?\\b","\\brecording angels?\\b","\\bwho are munkar\\b","\\bangels?\\b"],t.s)
B.b6V=s(["\\b(?:game|story|stories|angel investor)\\b"],t.s)
B.an7=new A.aN("angels-jibreel",B.bl4,B.b6V,"Angels are creatures of Allah, made from light, who obey Him and do what they are told: \"angels, harsh and severe; they do not disobey Allah in what He commands them but do what they are commanded\" (Qur'an 66:6). A'isha reported the Prophet said the angels were created from light, the jinn from the spark of fire, and Adam from what has been described to you (Sahih Muslim 2996). They are not male or female, and not partners with Allah.\n\nJibreel (Gabriel) is the angel of revelation who brought the Qur'an to the Prophet \ufdfa: \"Whoever is an enemy to Gabriel - it is [none but] he who has brought the Qur'an down upon your heart\" (Qur'an 2:97). He also came in the form of a man to teach the Companions their religion, asking about Islam, iman and ihsan (Sahih Muslim 8). Mikail (Michael) is named in Qur'an 2:98.\n\nOther angels do other tasks: recording deeds, protecting, taking souls, and guarding Paradise and the Fire. The Qur'an and hadith do not give details of every one, so the guidance is to believe in what is told and not to guess beyond it. Belief in the angels is the second article of iman.\n\nSource: Qur'an 66:6, 2:97, 2:98; Sahih Muslim 2996, 8.","angels",!0,"")
B.b2N=s(["\\bwhat happens (?:after|when) (?:you |we |a person |someone )?(?:die|death|dying)\\b","\\bafter death\\b","\\bafterlife\\b","\\bthe hereafter\\b","\\bwhat is barzakh\\b","\\bbarzakh\\b","\\bgrave\\b.*\\b(?:torment|questioning|punishment|life)\\b","\\bday of judg(?:e)?ment\\b","\\bjudgment day\\b","\\bresurrection\\b","\\bhow do muslims believe (?:about|in) death\\b","\\bakhirah\\b","\\bakhira\\b","\\bwhat is paradise\\b","\\bwhat is jannah\\b","\\bwhat is hell\\b","\\bwhat is jahannam\\b","\\bwhat is the day of resurrection\\b","\\bis there life after death\\b","\\bheaven and hell\\b","\\bwill i go to (?:heaven|hell|paradise|jannah|jahannam)\\b","\\bscales\\b.*\\b(?:deeds|judg\\w*|mizan)\\b","\\bmizan\\b","\\bsirat\\b"],t.s)
B.biG=s(["\\b(?:my|his|her|our) (?:father|mother|dad|mom|son|daughter|husband|wife|brother|sister|friend|grandfather|grandmother) (?:died|passed|is dead|has died)\\b","\\bfuneral\\b"],t.s)
B.alU=new A.aN("afterlife-death",B.b2N,B.biG,"Muslims believe that death is not the end but the move to the next stage. Here is what the Qur'an and hadith tell us.\n\n- Death: the soul is taken, and the person enters the barzakh, a barrier between this life and the Day of Resurrection. The Qur'an says of those who wish to return: \"No! It is only a word he is saying; and behind them is a barrier until the Day they are resurrected\" (Qur'an 23:100).\n- Resurrection: all people will be raised, and each will be reckoned. \"And We place the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection, so no soul will be treated unjustly at all. And if there is [even] the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it forth.\" (Qur'an 21:47)\n- Accountability: \"So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, And whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.\" (Qur'an 99:7-8)\n- Then Paradise (Jannah) for the believers and the Fire (Jahannam) for those who reject and do wrong, subject to Allah's mercy and justice. Belief in the Last Day is the fifth article of iman (Sahih Muslim 8).\n\nDetails such as the questioning in the grave and the bridge are reported in authentic hadith but are matters of the unseen, so we believe in what is told and do not argue about how. Allah is the Most Merciful: \"do not despair of the mercy of Allah\" (Qur'an 39:53).\n\nSource: Qur'an 23:100, 21:47, 99:7-8, 39:53; Sahih Muslim 8.\n[GO:/academy/aqeedah]","afterlife",!0,"")
B.aGZ=s(["\\bmahdi\\b","\\bal mahdi\\b","\\bimam mahdi\\b","\\bthe expected one\\b","\\bwho is the mahdi\\b","\\bwill the mahdi come\\b"],t.s)
B.alf=new A.aN("mahdi",B.aGZ,B.b,'The Mahdi ("the guided one") is a man from the Prophet\'s family who, according to reports, will appear near the end of time and fill the earth with justice. The reports are in Abu Dawud: Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated the Prophet said if only one day of this time remained, Allah would raise up a man from my family who would fill this earth with justice as it has been filled with oppression (Sunan Abu Dawud 4283, sahih per al-Albani).\n\nPlease note:\n- The reports come with different details (name, signs, timing). Scholars differ on how strong they are, and some doubt them. Sunni and Shia traditions also describe him differently.\n- Belief in the Mahdi is not one of the six articles of faith. A Muslim is not asked to look for him.\n- Be careful of anyone who claims to be the Mahdi, or says the signs have appeared. Many such claims have misled people. The Prophet \ufdfa spoke of Isa ibn Maryam too, who will return as a just ruler (Sahih al-Bukhari 3448).\n\nSource: Sunan Abu Dawud 4283, sahih per al-Albani; Sahih al-Bukhari 3448.',"mahdi",!0,"")
B.bfP=s(["\\bseek knowledge (?:even )?(?:as far as|even in|even unto|to) china\\b","\\bknowledge (?:even )?(?:in|as far as|to) china\\b","\\bchina\\b.*\\b(?:knowledge|hadith)\\b","\\b(?:knowledge|hadith)\\b.*\\bchina\\b","\\bseek(?:ing)? knowledge\\b.*\\b(?:hadith|authentic|sahih)\\b"],t.s)
B.boa=s(["\\bhadith (?:number|no|num)\\b"],t.s)
B.alM=new A.aN("china-knowledge",B.bfP,B.boa,'The saying "Seek knowledge even in China" is not an authentic hadith. It is not found in Bukhari, Muslim or the other major collections, and hadith scholars treat it as weak or invented, so it should not be attributed to the Prophet \ufdfa. It is often quoted for the real point that knowledge is worth travelling for.\n\nWhat is established is that Islam values knowledge highly. Allah says: "Are those who know equal to those who do not know" (Qur\'an 39:9), and told the Prophet \ufdfa to ask "My Lord, increase me in knowledge" (Qur\'an 20:114). Abu Hurayrah reported the Prophet said whoever treads a path seeking knowledge, Allah makes the way to Paradise easy for him (Sahih Muslim 2699).\n\nThe Seeking Knowledge guide in this app has authentic texts on the subject.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 39:9, 20:114; Sahih Muslim 2699.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-knowledge]',"knowledge",!0,"")
B.aNd=s(["\\bis seeking knowledge (?:obligatory|a duty|an obligation|fard|compulsory)\\b","\\bseeking knowledge (?:is|an?) (?:obligatory|duty|obligation|fard)\\b","\\bislam and (?:education|knowledge|science)\\b","\\bimportance of (?:knowledge|education|learning)\\b","\\bwhat does islam say about (?:knowledge|education|learning|studying|science)\\b","^seeking knowledge$","\\bis (?:education|studying|learning) important in islam\\b","\\bvalue of (?:knowledge|education)\\b"],t.s)
B.aLg=s(["\\bchina\\b","\\bhadith (?:number|no|num)\\b","\\bgames?\\b"],t.s)
B.amp=new A.aN("knowledge-importance",B.aNd,B.aLg,'Islam places great value on knowledge. The first word revealed to the Prophet \ufdfa was "Recite in the name of your Lord who created" (Qur\'an 96:1). Allah says: "Are those who know equal to those who do not know" (Qur\'an 39:9), and told the Prophet \ufdfa to ask "My Lord, increase me in knowledge" (Qur\'an 20:114). He also says that "Allah will raise those who have believed among you and those who were given knowledge, by degrees" (Qur\'an 58:11).\n\nAbu Hurayrah reported the Prophet said whoever treads a path seeking knowledge, Allah makes the way to Paradise easy for him (Sahih Muslim 2699).\n\nIs it a duty? Scholars agree that learning what you need in order to practise your religion (how to pray, fast, deal honestly and live) is a duty on every Muslim; deeper study is a duty on the community as a whole. A saying often quoted for this, "Seeking knowledge is a duty upon every Muslim", is Sunan Ibn Majah 224, da\'if per Darussalam. It is graded weak, so it is not used as evidence, though the meaning is agreed.\n\nThe Seeking Knowledge guide in this app has more.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 96:1, 39:9, 20:114, 58:11; Sahih Muslim 2699; Sunan Ibn Majah 224, da\'if per Darussalam.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-knowledge]',"knowledge",!0,"")
B.b5g=s(["\\bdoes allah (?:love|care about|hear|see|know|forgive|remember|accept) me\\b","\\bwill allah (?:love|forgive|accept|hear|help|punish|ever forgive) me\\b","\\bis allah (?:angry|upset|mad|disappointed|punishing|testing) (?:with|at) me\\b","\\bis allah (?:punishing|testing) me\\b","\\bdoes allah hate me\\b","\\ballah (?:hates|abandoned|forgot|left|ignores|ignored) me\\b","\\bwill allah ever forgive\\b","\\bdoes allah forgive (?:all|every|big|major|everything)\\b","\\bis there hope for me\\b","\\bi feel (?:far|distant) from allah\\b","\\bi feel allah (?:doesnt|does not|isnt) \\w+\\b","\\bcan allah forgive\\b","\\bi (?:committed|did) (?:a )?(?:big|major|terrible|huge|bad) sin\\b","\\bi m a (?:bad|terrible|sinful) muslim\\b"],t.s)
B.anj=new A.aN("allah-loves-me",B.b5g,B.b,'Allah is far more loving and merciful than we imagine, and He wants you to come back to Him. In a hard time He comforted His Prophet \ufdfa: "Your Lord has not taken leave of you" (Qur\'an 93:3), and His mercy is open to every servant who turns to Him.\n\nHe describes Himself as "the Forgiving, the Affectionate" (Qur\'an 85:14), and says "My mercy encompasses all things" (Qur\'an 7:156). The Prophet \ufdfa once saw a mother who found her child among the captives and held him to her chest, and asked his companions if they thought she would throw her child in the fire. They said no. The Prophet said Allah is more merciful to His slaves than this lady is to her son (Sahih al-Bukhari 5999).\n\nIf you have sinned, even greatly, the door is open: "do not despair of the mercy of Allah" (Qur\'an 39:53). Repentance (tawbah) is to stop the sin, feel regret, ask Allah to forgive you, resolve not to return, and, if you wronged a person, put the wrong right. Allah loves this: "Indeed, Allah loves those who are constantly repentant and loves those who purify themselves" (Qur\'an 2:222). Start by praying, making du\'a in your own words, and doing a small good deed today. If you are feeling lost, hopeless or in pain, please also talk with someone you trust.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 93:3, 85:14, 7:156, 39:53, 2:222; Sahih al-Bukhari 5999.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-tawba]',"mercy",!0,"")
B.aW_=s(["\\bis islam (?:a )?(?:religion of )?(?:peace|violent|violence|peaceful|terroris\\w*)\\b","\\bdoes islam (?:promote|teach|allow|encourage|support|permit) (?:violence|terroris\\w*|killing|war|murder)\\b","\\bwhat is jihad\\b","\\bmeaning of jihad\\b","\\bjihad\\b","\\bterroris\\w*\\b.*\\b(?:islam|muslims?)\\b","\\b(?:islam|muslims?)\\b.*\\bterroris\\w*\\b","\\bislam and (?:violence|terror\\w*|war)\\b","\\bkill(?:ing)? (?:non muslims?|infidels?|kafirs?|innocent)\\b","^peace$","\\bwhat does islam say about (?:violence|war|killing|peace)\\b","\\bis it (?:halal|allowed|permissible) to kill\\b","\\bsword verse\\b","\\bfight (?:the )?(?:infidels?|disbelievers|non muslims?)\\b"],t.s)
B.akU=new A.aN("jihad-peace",B.aW_,B.b,'Islam\'s teaching is to protect life and to be just to everyone. The Qur\'an says that killing an innocent person is like killing all of mankind: "whoever kills a soul unless for a soul or for corruption [done] in the land - it is as if he had slain mankind entirely. And whoever saves one - it is as if he had saved mankind entirely" (Qur\'an 5:32). Terror against civilians is a major sin and has no place in Islam, whoever does it and in whatever name.\n\nJihad means "striving". The greater part of it is the struggle against one\'s own desires and for good conduct. Fighting is permitted only in limited cases of defence against wrongs, with firm limits: "Fight in the way of Allah those who fight you but do not transgress. Indeed. Allah does not like transgressors" (Qur\'an 2:190), "Permission [to fight] has been given to those who are being fought, because they were wronged" (Qur\'an 22:39). The Prophet \ufdfa forbade the killing of women and children (Sahih al-Bukhari 3015), and warned against harming people under a treaty (Sahih al-Bukhari 3166).\n\nKindness to people of other faiths who do not fight you is commanded: "Allah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion and do not expel you from your homes - from being righteous toward them and acting justly toward them" (Qur\'an 60:8), and "There shall be no compulsion in [acceptance of] the religion" (Qur\'an 2:256). Whether any particular war is lawful is a question for qualified scholars, not for individuals or groups.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 5:32, 2:190, 22:39, 60:8, 2:256; Sahih al-Bukhari 3015, 3166.',"peace",!0,"")
B.aYu=s(["\\bis (?:christianity|judaism|hinduism|buddhism|sikhism|atheism|catholicism|christian\\w*) (?:true|right|correct|the truth|false|wrong|the true religion)\\b","\\b(?:do|did) you think (?:that )?(?:christianity|judaism|hinduism|buddhism|atheism|islam|christians|jews) (?:is|are) (?:true|right|correct)\\b","\\bwhich (?:religion|faith) is (?:true|right|correct|the truth|the best|better)\\b","\\bis islam (?:the )?(?:only )?(?:true|right|correct|best|only) (?:religion|way|faith)\\b","\\bis islam (?:the )?(?:only|one) (?:way|path|religion)\\b","\\bwhy (?:islam|is islam|should i choose islam|choose islam|be a muslim)\\b","\\bwhat does islam say about (?:christians?|jews?|hindus?|buddhists?|atheists?|other religions|non muslims?|people of other faiths)\\b","\\bwill (?:non muslims?|christians?|jews?|hindus?|atheists?|people of other (?:faiths?|religions?)) go to (?:hell|heaven|paradise|jahannam|jannah)\\b","\\bdo (?:muslims|you) respect (?:other religions|christians|jews)\\b","\\bis jesus (?:god|the son of god|divine)\\b","\\btrinity\\b","\\bwhat do muslims (?:believe|think) about (?:jesus|isa|christ)\\b","\\bdid jesus die on the cross\\b","\\bcrucifix\\w*\\b","\\bwhat is the difference between islam and christianity\\b","\\bislam (?:vs|versus|and) christianity\\b"],t.s)
B.alq=new A.aN("other-religions",B.aYu,B.b,'I answer from Islam, so I can tell you what Muslims believe, and I will not mock or attack anyone\'s faith.\n\nMuslims believe that Allah sent messengers to every people with one message, to worship Him alone, and that Muhammad \ufdfa is the last of them. So Muslims say that the religion with Allah is Islam, meaning submission to Him ("Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam" (Qur\'an 3:19)), the way of Ibrahim: "Abraham was neither a Jew nor a Christian, but he was one inclining toward truth, a Muslim [submitting to Allah]" (Qur\'an 3:67).\n\nOn Jesus (Isa): Muslims honour him as one of the greatest messengers, born miraculously to Maryam, and a word from Allah. The Qur\'an says: "The Messiah, Jesus, the son of Mary, was but a messenger of Allah and His word which He directed to Mary and a soul [created at a command] from Him" (Qur\'an 4:171), and teaches that he is not God or the son of God, and rejects the Trinity, and says that to claim Allah is the third of three is disbelief: "And there is no god except one God" (Qur\'an 5:73). The Qur\'an also compares his creation to that of Adam (Qur\'an 3:59). So Muslims and Christians agree on his honour and miracles, and differ on who he is.\n\nHow Muslims are told to treat others: "There shall be no compulsion in [acceptance of] the religion" (Qur\'an 2:256), "do not argue with the People of the Scripture except in a way that is best" (Qur\'an 29:46), and in the last words of Surah Al-Kafirun: "For you is your religion, and for me is my religion" (Qur\'an 109:6). Whom Allah admits to Paradise is for Him to judge; a Muslim\'s duty is to invite with kindness and wisdom and to be just to everyone.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 3:19, 3:67, 4:171, 5:73, 3:59, 2:256, 29:46, 109:6.',"religions",!0,"")
B.aRK=s(["\\bwho are you\\b","\\bwho is hadi\\b","\\bwhat (?:is|s) hadi\\b","\\bwhat are you\\b","^hadi$","\\bwhat does hadi mean\\b","^(?:tell me about )?(?:yourself|hadi)\\b","\\bintroduce yourself\\b"],t.s)
B.Qb=s(["\\b(?:hits?|beats?|divorce|talaq|my husband|my wife)\\b"],t.s)
B.amo=new A.aN("hadi-who",B.aRK,B.Qb,'I am Hadi, the guide in Ar-Rayaan. The name means "the guide". I answer from a library built into the app: the Qur\'an, the six hadith collections and the app\'s own guides, and every answer shows where it comes from.\n\nI am an app, not a person, and not a scholar. If you want to know what I can help with, ask "what can you do".\n[GO:/sources]',"about hadi",!0,"")
B.bbK=s(["\\bwho made you\\b","\\bwho (?:built|created|developed|designed|programmed|wrote|coded|owns|trained|invented) (?:you|hadi)\\b","\\bwho is your (?:maker|creator|developer|owner|author)\\b","\\bwho are your (?:makers?|creators?|developers?|owners?)\\b","\\bwho is behind (?:you|hadi)\\b","\\bwho (?:wrote|writes) your answers\\b"],t.s)
B.ano=new A.aN("hadi-maker",B.bbK,B.b,"I am part of Ar-Rayaan, which is an app of RHW Technologies. Its owner is Abdul G Khokhar. That is what the app states, and it is all I know about who is behind me: it gives no funder, address or company details, so I will not guess any.\n\nMy answers are not written one by one by a person while we talk. They come from a library built into the app, and each one shows the Qur'an verse or hadith it rests on. No scholar has reviewed the library yet, and the app says so on its Sources page.\n[GO:/sources]","about hadi",!0,"")
B.b0H=s(["\\b(?:are you|is hadi|is this|r u)\\b.*\\b(?:openai|open ai|chatgpt|chat gpt|gpt|gemini|claude|anthropic|grok|llama|deepseek|copilot|bard|mistral|an llm|a language model)\\b","\\b(?:you|hadi|this app|the app)\\b.*\\b(?:made|built|powered|run|running|trained|based|created|developed|using|uses|use)\\b.*\\b(?:openai|open ai|chatgpt|chat gpt|gpt|gemini|claude|anthropic|grok|llama|deepseek|copilot|bard|mistral)\\b","\\bwhat (?:ai|model|llm|language model|technology|engine) (?:are you|do you use|is this|is hadi|are you using|powers you|do you run on|is behind you)\\b","\\bwhich (?:ai|model|llm|language model) (?:are you|do you use|is this|is hadi|powers you)\\b","\\bwhat powers you\\b","\\bare you (?:powered|run) by\\b","\\bare you (?:an? )?(?:llm|large language model|neural network)\\b"],t.s)
B.anf=new A.aN("hadi-model",B.b0H,B.b,'No. I am not made by OpenAI or by any other AI company, and the app names no model for me. By default my answers come from a library built into the app: the Qur\'an, the six hadith collections and the app\'s own guides, matched to your question on your device, with the source printed under each answer.\n\nTwo things are optional, and both are off unless you turn them on:\n- If you add your own AI account (in my menu, "Your own AI account"), your questions then go to the provider you chose, under that provider\'s terms. Those replies are not from the library and have not been reviewed.\n- In Settings, under Support and wellbeing, "Use the online model for support chats" is off by default. Only if you turn it on can what you type in a support chat be sent to the online model Ar-Rayaan is connected to. It is never used when a message looks like an emergency or abuse, or when a child is speaking, and your own AI key is never used for it.\n\nThe Privacy policy in Settings lists every outside service the app can reach.\n[GO:/settings]\n[GO:/sources]',"about hadi",!0,"")
B.bmH=s(["^(?:can you )?(?:issue|give|make) (?:me )?(?:a )?fatwa\\b","\\b(?:give|issue|make|write) (?:me )?(?:a )?fatwa\\b","\\bi (?:want|need) (?:a )?fatwa\\b","\\bwhat is a fatwa\\b.*\\byou\\b","\\bdo you give fatwas?\\b","^(?:can you )?give (?:islamic )?rulings?\\b","\\bare you (?:a )?(?:mufti|qualified to give fatwas?)\\b"],t.s)
B.alG=new A.aN("hadi-fatwa",B.bmH,B.b,"I cannot give a fatwa. A fatwa is a ruling from a qualified mufti who knows your situation and can ask you questions, and I am an app with a library, not a mufti.\n\nWhat I can do is show you what the Qur'an and the hadith say on a question, with the source and the hadith grade, and say where the four schools differ. That is a study aid, not a ruling for your case.\n\nFor a ruling on your own situation, such as a marriage, a debt, an inheritance or whether your worship is valid, ask a qualified scholar of your school in person. \"Your school of law\" in my menu lets me name your school when I point you to one, and the Huda guides show each guide's school note.\n[GO:/huda]\n[GO:/sources]","about hadi",!0,"")
B.aKn=s(["\\bwhat can (?:you|hadi) do\\b","\\bwhat (?:do|can) you (?:help|know)\\b","\\bhow can you help\\b","\\bwhat can i ask\\b","\\bwhat should i ask\\b","\\bhelp me\\b$","^help$","\\bwhat topics\\b","\\bwhat do you cover\\b","\\bwhat are your (?:features|abilities|capabilities)\\b","\\bhow (?:do|does) (?:you|hadi) work\\b","\\bare you (?:an? )?(?:ai|bot|robot|human|real|person|scholar|sheikh|shaykh|imam|mufti|alim)\\b","\\bis this (?:an? )?(?:ai|bot|human|person)\\b","\\bcan i trust you\\b","\\bare you reliable\\b","\\bare your answers (?:correct|right|accurate|reliable)\\b","^(?:can you )?make mistakes\\b","\\bdo you make mistakes\\b"],t.s)
B.alk=new A.aN("hadi-about",B.aKn,B.Qb,'I am Hadi, the guide inside this app. I am not a scholar, a sheikh or a mufti, and I cannot issue a fatwa. I answer from a built-in library of the Qur\'an and the Sunnah, show where each answer comes from (the source card gives the collection, the number, and for hadith the grade and who graded it), and take you to the right screen of the app.\n\nI can help with:\n- Worship: wudu, ghusl, prayer, fasting, zakat, Hajj and Umrah, funerals.\n- What is halal and haram in food, money and everyday life, and family and marriage questions.\n- The basics of belief, the Prophet\'s life, the companions and Islamic history.\n- Du\'as, and where to find things in the app: Qur\'an, Prayer Times, Qibla, Games, the Academy and more.\n\nWho made the app: RHW Technologies. The owner is Abdul G Khokhar.\n\nWho has reviewed this: no one yet. The app\'s own words are "Scholar review needed. No named scholar has reviewed this app yet. We check every citation we can, we say so when we cannot, and we will name a reviewer here only once one has agreed to be named."\n\nWhere the schools of law differ, I say so and do not pick one for you. For a ruling on your own case (a divorce, an inheritance, a debt), I will not guess: a qualified scholar who can ask you questions must answer. I can be wrong, so please treat my answers as a study aid and check the source. If I do not know something, I say so.\n\nI answer in English only. Ask me anything about Islam or the app, for example "how many rak\'ahs is Fajr", "is gelatin halal" or "how do I play Ludo".\n[GO:/sources]',"about hadi",!0,"")
B.aH2=s(["\\bstreaks?\\b","\\bpoints?\\b.*\\b(?:app|hadi|game|games|quran|prayer|worship|earn|get|score|reward)\\b","\\b(?:app|hadi|game|games|worship)\\b.*\\bpoints?\\b","\\bcoins?\\b","\\bbadges?\\b","\\bleaderboards?\\b","\\blevels? up\\b","\\bgamif\\w*\\b","\\bdays returned\\b","\\bcome back (?:streak|calendar)\\b","\\breward(?:s)? (?:in|for) the app\\b","\\bdoes the app (?:track|count|score)\\b","\\bwhat is keep my streaks\\b","\\bturn (?:off|on) streaks?\\b","\\bkeep a private log\\b","\\bmy log\\b","\\bprivate log\\b"],t.s)
B.bkB=s(["\\b(?:good deeds?|hasanat|hasanah|reward from allah|reward in|rewards? of)\\b"],t.s)
B.amK=new A.aN("tracking-points",B.aH2,B.bkB,'Ar-Rayaan does not count days in a row, and nothing in it starts over when you take a break. If you like, you can keep a private log: the switch is called "Keep a private log", in Settings under "Coming back" and on the My log screen.\n\nWhen it is on, the app adds up what you read in the Qur\'an, your dhikr and tasbeeh and your lessons. My log also reads your own prayer log and fasting log. You see plain totals for this week, this month and all time, the last day you logged, and a calendar of the days you logged. A day with nothing on it is just empty space. It all stays on your device and is never shared.\n\nThere are no points, coins, ranks or leaderboards for worship anywhere in the app, and no scolding when you have been away: when you come back you are simply welcomed. If you switch the log off, the days it saved for Qur\'an, dhikr and lessons are erased; your prayer log and fasting log stay as they are.\n[GO:/my-log]\n[GO:/settings]',"my log",!0,"")
B.aTX=s(["\\b(?:change|switch|set|choose|pick|select|use) (?:the |my )?(?:app )?language\\b","\\blanguage (?:of|in|for|settings?|options?|menu)\\b.*\\b(?:app|hadi)\\b","\\b(?:app|hadi)\\b.*\\blanguages?\\b","\\bis (?:the )?(?:app|hadi) (?:available|translated|offered) in\\b","\\b(?:does|can) (?:the )?(?:app|hadi) (?:speak|understand|support|answer in|reply in|work in|talk in)\\b","\\b(?:app|hadi) in (?:urdu|arabic|bangla|bengali|french|turkish|malay|indonesian|hindi|spanish|german|english)\\b","\\b(?:urdu|arabic|bangla|bengali|french|turkish|malay|indonesian|hindi|spanish|german) (?:version|language|translation|support)\\b.*\\b(?:app|hadi)\\b","\\btranslate the app\\b","\\blanguage and voice\\b","\\blanguage \\& voice\\b","\\bwhich languages\\b","\\bwhat languages\\b","\\bavailable languages\\b","\\bvoice (?:reading|read aloud|reader)\\b","\\bread (?:it |answers? |text )?aloud\\b","\\btext to speech\\b","\\bmy language\\b"],t.s)
