B.anm=new A.aN("downloads-offline",B.b2R,B.b6t,"Most of the app works without the internet. The Qur'an text, the stories, the guides and the duas are already inside the app. What you can download is recitation audio, so you can listen with no connection.\n\nTo do it, open Downloads (from the menu). Pick a reciter and download a surah or more; each row shows its size, whether it is waiting, downloading, paused or on your device. A few points:\n- Downloads are for the reciter you have chosen only; change the reciter on that screen if you want another.\n- \"Wi-Fi only\" is a switch so that big downloads wait for Wi-Fi and do not use mobile data. Your phone only guesses which network it is on, so check before a big download.\n- You can pause at any time and delete any download later to free the space.\n- In a web browser, downloads are kept in the browser's storage. Once you have opened the app online, the browser also keeps a copy of the app itself, so it can reopen with no internet (not in a private window, and not after you clear the site data). The Android app keeps everything on the phone and opens with no internet.\n[GO:/downloads]","downloads",!0,"")
B.biW=s(["\\b(?:kids?|children|child) (?:section|mode|corner|area|zone|page|part|feature|profile|profiles|friendly|safe)\\b","\\bfor children\\b","\\bis (?:the )?app (?:safe|suitable|ok|okay|good) for (?:kids?|children|my (?:kid|child|son|daughter))\\b","\\b(?:kids?|children) (?:in|on) (?:the )?app\\b","\\bmy (?:kid|kids|child|children|son|daughter)s? (?:use|using|play|playing|learn|learning)\\b.*\\bapp\\b","\\bparental (?:controls?|gate|check)\\b","\\bfamily wing\\b","\\bchild profiles?\\b","\\bwhere (?:are|is) (?:the )?(?:kids?|children)\\b","\\bapp for (?:kids?|children)\\b","\\bteach (?:my )?(?:kids?|children) (?:with|using|in) (?:the )?app\\b","\\bletters? for (?:kids?|children)\\b"],t.s)
B.aVk=s(["\\b(?:how to raise|parenting|discipline|hit|beat|spank|pray at what age|what age)\\b"],t.s)
B.alP=new A.aN("kids-help",B.biW,B.aVk,'The For Children section has three doors: the Arabic letters (learn them one at a time), Games (play and learn), and the Stories school (stories with a lesson to talk about). On the Home screen it is the "For Children" tile. A grown-up can sit with the child.\n\nAbout privacy: the app is a general-audience app and is not directed to children under 13. In the Family Wing a parent can add child profiles that keep only a first name or nickname and the child\'s progress in the Arabic letters, and they stay on the device. No age, photo, voice, e-mail, phone number or location is asked for. Adding or removing a child sits behind a parent check. The online game tables (Ludo and Shatranj with a friend, using a six-letter code) are off for every child unless a parent switches them on. The full text is in the Privacy policy screen.\n[GO:/academy/family]',"kids",!0,"")
B.b0Q=s(["\\b(?:change|switch|set|choose|pick|select|update|find|where is|how do i set)\\b.*\\b(?:my )?(?:school of (?:law|thought)|madhhab|madhab|mazhab)\\b","\\b(?:my )?(?:school of (?:law|thought)|madhhab)\\b.*\\b(?:setting|settings|menu|app|hadi|change|set|choose|select)\\b","\\bwhich school (?:does|do) (?:hadi|you|the app) follow\\b","\\bwhat madhhab (?:are you|is hadi|does hadi)\\b","\\bare you (?:hanafi|shafii|maliki|hanbali|sunni|shia)\\b","\\bset (?:to )?(?:hanafi|shafii|maliki|hanbali)\\b","\\bhanafi (?:mode|setting)\\b","\\bwhy does hadi (?:ask|say) .*school\\b"],t.s)
B.an9=new A.aN("school-setting",B.b0Q,B.b,'Open the Hadi screen, tap the menu in the corner and choose "Your school of law". You can pick Not sure, Hanafi, Shafi\'i, Maliki or Hanbali. It is kept on your device only.\n\nWhat it changes: where the four schools differ, I name your school\'s view first and say plainly that other schools differ. I never say another school is wrong. If you pick "Not sure", I say that the schools differ and do not pick one for you. Where I do not hold a verified text for a single school, I say that and point you to a scholar of your school.\n\nI answer from the Sunni tradition: the Qur\'an and the Sunnah, with the four Sunni schools of law. I am a study aid, not a mufti.',"madhhab setting",!0,"")
B.b8o=s(["\\bis (?:my )?(?:data|privacy|information|chat|chats|conversation|conversations|messages?) (?:private|safe|secure|stored|shared|sold|saved|recorded|tracked|kept)\\b","\\b(?:privacy|privacy policy|terms of service|terms and conditions)\\b","\\bdo you (?:track|store|save|record|sell|share|collect|log) (?:my |our )?(?:data|chats?|conversations?|messages?|questions?|location)\\b","\\bwho (?:sees|reads|can see|can read) (?:my )?(?:chats?|questions?|messages?|data|conversations?)\\b","\\bdoes (?:the )?app (?:have|show|contain|run) (?:ads|adverts|advertising|advertisements)\\b","\\bany ads\\b","\\badvert\\w*\\b","\\bis (?:the )?app (?:free|paid|premium|subscription)\\b","\\bis (?:this|it) (?:free|paid)\\b","\\bhow much (?:does|do|is) (?:the )?(?:app|it) cost\\b","\\b(?:subscription|premium|pro version|in app purchase|paywall|pricing|price of the app)\\b","\\bwho (?:owns|runs|made|built|funds) (?:the |this )?app\\b","\\bwho is behind (?:the )?app\\b","\\bdelete (?:my )?(?:account|data|history|chats?|conversation|conversations)\\b","\\bclear (?:my )?(?:chat|history|conversations?|data)\\b","\\bdo i need (?:an? )?(?:account|login|sign ?up|api key)\\b","\\bsign in\\b","\\bapi key\\b","\\bis (?:it|hadi) online\\b","\\bdoes hadi (?:need|use|work) (?:the )?(?:internet|online|api|ai)\\b","\\bis (?:hadi|this) (?:an? )?(?:offline|online)\\b"],t.s)
B.bg8=s(["\\boffline\\b","\\b(?:who (?:runs|owns|funds|pays for|is behind|made|built|created)|owner of|funded|funds it|funding|company behind)\\b","\\b(?:data of|big data|quran data)\\b"],t.s)
B.alJ=new A.aN("privacy-free-ads",B.b8o,B.bg8,'What I can tell you, from the app\'s own Privacy policy screen:\n- Your settings, bookmarks, progress, reflections and saved conversations with me are stored on your device. You can clear them by clearing the app\'s data.\n- I answer from a library built into the app, which does not leave your device. Only if you choose to add your own key for an AI provider are your key and the messages of that conversation sent to that provider, under its terms. Messages that look like a personal crisis are answered on the device and are not sent or saved.\n- Accounts: if you create one, sign-in uses Firebase Authentication. You can delete your account and data from Settings: the "Delete my account" link opens the Delete account screen. What you post in the Majlis is public.\n- Prayer times, Qibla and the mosque finder use the location you give or allow; the app contacts services such as prayer-time and map services and audio servers to work.\n- The policy says: "We do not sell personal data or show advertising based on it."\n\nWhat I cannot tell you: I do not have a price list or a statement about future plans, so I will not guess whether anything will be paid or free later. The Terms and Privacy screens are the place to read the exact words; the policy there is marked as a draft.',"privacy",!0,"")
B.aWQ=s(["\\bwho is wasia\\b","\\bwhat is wasia\\b","\\bwhos wasia\\b","^wasia$","^(?:tell me about )?wasia\\b","\\bis wasia (?:real|a person|an ai|a robot|ai)\\b"],t.s)
B.ana=new A.aN("wasia-who",B.aWQ,B.b,"Wasia is the AI teacher of the Wasia Academy, the letter school built with love. She teaches the Arabic alphabet, reads with the child, and speaks in three voices: student, parent, and a Teachers' Corner for parents. Shall I take you there?\n[GO:/academy/gate]","academy",!0,"")
B.b4N=s(["\\bwhat is (?:the )?(?:wasia )?academy\\b","\\bwasia\\b","\\b(?:wasia )?academy\\b.*\\b(?:what|how|where|start|begin|open|lessons?|courses?|schools?)\\b","\\bhow (?:do|to|can) i (?:start|begin|use) (?:the )?academy\\b","\\bwhere (?:is|are) (?:the )?(?:academy|lessons|courses)\\b","\\bi want to learn (?:islam|arabic|quran|prayer)\\b.*\\bapp\\b","\\bwhat (?:lessons|courses|schools) (?:are|do you have|does the app have)\\b","\\bletter school\\b","\\bschool of letters\\b","\\bteacher in the app\\b"],t.s)
B.bhW=s(["\\b(?:hifz|memori[sz]e)\\b"],t.s)
B.alR=new A.aN("academy-help",B.b4N,B.bhW,'The Wasia Academy is the learning part of the app. It is on the Home screen as "Wasia Academy: learn with your teacher". It opens the school of Arabic letters, with Wasia as your teacher, and the other schools for learning step by step, such as Qur\'anic Arabic, Aqeedah, Seerah, Hadith, Family life, Ramadan Mode, Hifz and Hajj and Umrah.\n\nStart with the Arabic letters if you are a beginner. A parent can set up child profiles in the Family Wing. For a quick answer rather than a course, ask me.\n[GO:/academy]',"academy",!0,"")
B.blq=s(["\\bhow (?:does|do) (?:scoring|score|scores|points|winning) work\\b","\\bscoring\\b","\\bhow (?:do|to) (?:i )?win\\b","\\bhow does (?:the )?game (?:end|work)\\b","\\bhints?\\b.*\\bgame\\b","\\bis there a timer\\b","\\bgame (?:settings?|options?)\\b","\\bresume\\b","\\bcontinue (?:a |my |the )?(?:game|playing)\\b","\\bfinish (?:a |my |the )?game\\b","\\bunfinished game\\b","\\bgame history\\b","\\bmy (?:game )?history\\b","\\bpast games\\b","\\bprevious games\\b","\\bwhere (?:is|are) my (?:game|games|results?|history|score|scores)\\b","\\bsaved games?\\b","\\bpractice (?:with|a) friend\\b","\\bplay (?:with|against) (?:a )?friend\\b","\\bplay online\\b"],t.s)
B.b2w=s(["\\b(?:chess|shatranj|ludo|memory|trivia|timeline|names|lineage|hijrah|word|quran knowledge|stories trivia|hifz)\\b"],t.s)
B.amU=new A.aN("games-general",B.blq,B.b2w,'The Games screen lists every game that works today, in four groups: Islamic (such as Qur\'an Knowledge, Stories Trivia, the 99 Names, Lineage Challenge and the Hijrah Journey), Strategy (Shatranj, which is chess), Family (Ludo) and Words and puzzles. Ask me about a game by name, for example "how do I play Ludo", and I will tell you the rules and how to start.\n\nScoring: the quizzes show how many you got right out of the total, and after each answer you see the source. There is no timer in the quizzes. Hints are free: a hint hides two wrong answers, and you get three free hints in a game. Nothing is sold, and there are no ratings, coins or leaderboards. Memorising the Qur\'an in Hifz practice has no score.\n\nA game you started and did not finish is shown at the top of the Games screen under "Continue playing". Finished games appear in Game history (button at the bottom of the Games screen), which is kept on this device only; you can clear it there. Playing Ludo or Shatranj with a friend on another device uses a six-letter code and needs the internet and the online hall to be switched on; if it is not, the app tells you.\n[GO:/games]\n[GO:/games/history]',"games",!0,"")
B.aOH=s(["\\b(?:grade|grading|rating|status|authenticity|strength|classification)\\b.*\\b(?:hadith|saying|narration)\\b","\\b(?:hadith|saying|narration)\\b.*\\b(?:grade|graded|rated|authentic|authenticity|sahih|saheeh|hasan|daif|weak|fabricated|mawdu|forged|fake|invented|reliable|real|true|genuine)\\b","\\bis (?:this |the |that |it )?(?:hadith|saying|narration)\\b.*\\b(?:authentic|sahih|saheeh|hasan|daif|weak|fabricated|forged|fake|real|true|genuine|reliable|correct)\\b","\\bis it (?:an? )?(?:authentic|sahih|saheeh|weak|fabricated|real|genuine) (?:hadith|saying)\\b","\\bwhat is the (?:grade|status|ruling|authenticity) of\\b.*\\b(?:hadith|saying|actions are|intentions|narration)\\b","\\b(?:grade|status|rating) of (?:the )?(?:hadith|saying)\\b","\\bwhich hadith (?:are|is) (?:sahih|authentic|weak|fabricated)\\b","\\bhow (?:do|can) i (?:know|check|find out|verify) (?:if |whether )?(?:a |the |this )?(?:hadith|saying) is (?:authentic|sahih|real|true|weak)\\b"],t.s)
B.bnV=s(["\\bchina\\b","\\bhadith (?:number|no|num)\\b","\\bwhat is (?:a )?(?:sahih|hasan|daif|weak|fabricated|mawdu)\\b","\\bwhat does sahih mean\\b"],t.s)
B.all=new A.aN("hadith-grade-ask",B.aOH,B.bnV,'I do not grade hadith myself, and I will not give a grade from memory. A grade is a scholar\'s judgment on the chain and the text, and it can differ from one scholar to another.\n\nWhat I can do:\n- For hadith from Sahih al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim, the scholars accepted the collections as sound, so a report found in them is not given a separate grade there. Where this app prints a hadith from the other four books (Abu Dawud, at-Tirmidhi, an-Nasa\'i, Ibn Majah), it shows the grade and who gave it, for example "sahih per al-Albani". Look at the source card under an answer.\n- If you ask me about one hadith by its first words or its topic, I will tell you whether it is on my shelf and show its source and grade.\n- The Hadith screen holds the Forty Hadith of Imam an-Nawawi and a daily hadith, each with its collection, number and grade where one is on file.\n- To check a saying you have seen online, search its words in the collections; if it is in none of the six books, be careful with it. A qualified scholar, or a hadith database that names the scholar who graded it, is the place to confirm it.\n\nOne example I do hold: "Actions are only by intentions" is in Sahih al-Bukhari (number 1) and in Sahih Muslim (number 1907), so it is among the most firmly established of all hadith. And "Seek knowledge even in China" is not an authentic hadith (ask me about it by name).\n[GO:/hadith]\n[GO:/search]',"hadith",!0,"")
B.blN=s(["\\bdifference between\\b.*\\b(?:fard|farz|wajib|sunnah|nafl|mustahabb)\\b","\\b(?:fard|farz|wajib|mustahabb|nafl)\\b","\\bwhat (?:is|does) (?:fard|farz|wajib|sunnah mu?akkadah|makruh|mubah)\\b","\\bmeaning of (?:fard|farz|wajib|makruh|mubah|mustahabb|haram|halal)\\b","\\btypes? of (?:rulings?|actions?)\\b","\\bfive (?:categories|rulings)\\b","\\bwhat is (?:the )?(?:difference|meaning) .*\\bsunnah\\b.*\\bnafl\\b","\\bwhat (?:are|is) (?:the )?(?:categories|kinds|levels) of (?:ruling|obligation)\\b","\\bwhat does makruh mean\\b"],t.s)
B.aHl=s(["\\b(?:app|game)\\b"],t.s)
B.alQ=new A.aN("prayer-wajib-sunnah",B.blN,B.aHl,"Islamic law (fiqh) puts every action in one of these levels:\n- Fard (obligatory): required; reward for doing it, sin for leaving it. Examples: the five daily prayers, fasting Ramadan, zakat. A communal duty (fard kifayah) is one that is lifted from everyone once enough people do it, like the funeral prayer.\n- Wajib: in the Hanafi school, a duty just below fard (established by a text that is less certain), like witr and the Eid prayer; leaving it is sinful. The other schools treat wajib and fard as the same thing, except in Hajj.\n- Sunnah (recommended): what the Prophet \ufdfa did and encouraged; rewarded, and not sinful to leave. Sunnah mu'akkadah is a sunnah he rarely left, like the sunnah before Fajr.\n- Mustahabb / nafl (praiseworthy or voluntary): extra acts, rewarded, not emphasised.\n- Mubah (permitted): neither rewarded nor sinful.\n- Makruh (disliked): better to avoid; not sinful to do.\n- Haram (forbidden): sinful to do, rewarded to avoid for Allah's sake.\n\nNote that \"sunnah\" also means the whole way of the Prophet \ufdfa (his words, actions and approvals), which is the second source after the Qur'an.","fard wajib",!0,"")
