B.crA=new A.lT("Abu Bakr \u2014 The Steady One","The first caliph: 'If you worship Muhammad, know that he has died; but if you worship Allah, He lives and does not die.' He saved zakat and saved the deen in two years.","comp-abu-bakr")
B.crv=new A.lT("Umar \u2014 Justice on Horseback","The second caliph, who patrolled Medina at night and answered to no one but Allah \u2014 the milk-seller\u2019s story is his most told parable of fairness.","comp-umar")
B.cru=new A.lT("The Pot of Milk","A report (Muwatta Malik, through Zayd ibn Aslam) that Umar made himself vomit milk he learned came from the zakat camels. A report, not an eyewitness chain; scholar review needed.","tale-umar-milk")
B.crp=new A.lT("Uthman \u2014 The Gatherer of the Quran","The third caliph: gentle by nature, decisive when it mattered \u2014 he ordered the one mushaf, and the ummah has read from it ever since.","comp-uthman")
B.crw=new A.lT("Ali \u2014 Raised in the Prophet\u2019s House","The fourth caliph, raised in the Prophet\u2019s house \u2014 the era\u2019s scholarship begins with him.","comp-ali")
B.aWA=s([B.crA,B.crv,B.cru,B.crp,B.crw],t.rU)
B.crD=new A.SJ("The Rashidun \u2014 The Righteous Twenty-Nine Years","Abu Bakr saved the community from collapsing into apostasy in his two years. Umar spread justice so far the Nile is said to have blessed his letter. Uthman gathered the Quran into one book. Ali carried the law through the first fitna. Four caliphs, one standard: the Prophet\u2019s example, not their own ambition.",B.aWA)
B.crr=new A.lT("Uwais al-Qarni \u2014 Who Honored a Mother","He never met the Prophet \ufdfa, yet the Prophet praised him from afar \u2014 for how he treated his mother.","tale-uwais")
B.crq=new A.lT("Jurayj \u2014 The Ascetic and the Mother","His mother called him while he prayed, and heaven itself corrected him \u2014 worship never outranks the one who raised you.","tale-jurayj")
B.crs=new A.lT("Barsisa \u2014 A Tale We Cannot Verify","A monk\u2019s tale some commentaries tell about 59:16. The app does not retell it; it gives the Qur\u2019an\u2019s parable of Shaytan instead.","tale-barsisa")
B.crB=new A.lT("Khalid \u2014 Words on His Deathbed","The words reported on Khalid ibn al-Walid\u2019s deathbed (Ibn al-Athir, Usd al-Ghaba; a seerah report, not from the six books, scholar review needed).","tale-khalid-letter")
B.crC=new A.lT("The Boy-King \u2014 Which World Is Real?","The question that has launched a thousand history seminars: what if power, and not poverty, is the dream?","tale-boy-king")
B.aZD=s([B.crr,B.crq,B.crs,B.crB,B.crC],t.rU)
B.crE=new A.SJ("The Generations After \u2014 Scholars and Judges","From the generation after the companions come the judges, the ascetics, and the scholars whose names became disciplines. The library\u2019s Tales collection carries these voices.",B.aZD)
B.crx=new A.lT("Baghdad\u2019s House of Wisdom","In the 9th century, Baghdad\u2019s scholars translated the world\u2019s knowledge into Arabic \u2014 Greek philosophy, Indian mathematics, Persian medicine \u2014 and added to it algebra (al-Khwarizmi), optics (Ibn al-Haytham), and the hospitals. The empire\u2019s armies carried the message; its scholars carried the light.",null)
B.cry=new A.lT("Cordoba \u2014 The City of Light","While much of Europe\u2019s libraries were closed, Cordoba\u2019s were open \u2014 over 70,000 manuscripts, streetlights, and public baths, all while the Quran was recited in the Great Mosque. When the library of Cordoba was catalogued, it filled 44 volumes. The scholars outlived the swords.",null)
B.crz=new A.lT("The Ottoman Centuries","For 600 years, the Ottomans held the two Harams and the three continents \u2014 and their sultans slept in humility while the empire\u2019s greatest monuments were mosques and madrasas. The empire fell; the Quran it protected never did.",null)
B.crt=new A.lT("The Scholars Outlived the Empires","Empires rose on the map and vanished from it; the Quran, the hadith collections, and the law schools remained \u2014 and still govern the daily life of two billion people. Ibn Taymiyyah died in a citadel; Imam Ghazali died with his head on his books. Their works never died. That is the history worth remembering.",null)
B.b10=s([B.crx,B.cry,B.crz,B.crt],t.rU)
B.crF=new A.SJ("The Later Ages \u2014 Empires, Andalus, Ottoman","The story continues: Cordoba\u2019s libraries when Europe\u2019s were dark, Baghdad\u2019s House of Wisdom, the Ottoman centuries holding the two Harams. These eras are named here as the road ahead \u2014 the library\u2019s next historical chapters will walk them. What never changes: the carriers of this deen are remembered for their scholarship and their mercy, never their conquests.",B.b10)
B.bhd=s([B.crD,B.crE,B.crF],A.ab("A<SJ>"))
