B.WU=new A.T(B.byC,["A Debt That Purifies","Zakat joins salah in the Qur'an more than thirty times \u2014 'establish prayer and give zakah' (2:43). It is not a tip; it is a pillar with a name that means growth. Your wealth does not shrink by zakat \u2014 it is purified, and the promise attached to gratitude and giving is increase itself (14:7).","Open the Zakat Guide","Read how nisab, the lunar year, and the 2.5% rate work \u2014 then check whether your savings have passed the threshold.",u.bU,u.bU,"The Third Pillar","Eight Doors, One Verse","The Qur'an names zakat's recipients in a single verse (9:60): the poor, the needy, the administrators, those whose hearts are to be reconciled, freeing captives, the debt-ridden, in Allah's cause, and the stranded traveler. Your zakat is a targeted mercy, not a general donation.","Read: The Zakat Guide's Recipients Section","See each of the eight categories explained in plain words.",u.ru,u.ru,"Where Zakat Goes","The Grain That Multiplies","Allah compares the giver to a grain growing seven ears, each with a hundred grains (2:261). Voluntary charity has no rate, no season, no minimum \u2014 even a kind word is written as sadaqah. Start where the Prophet \ufdfa started: small, steady, often hidden.","One Hidden Coin This Week","Give something this week that no one but Allah sees \u2014 then tell no one.",u.A_,u.A_,"Sadaqah \u2014 The Voluntary River","Prescribed, Not Invented","'O you who have believed, decreed upon you is fasting as it was decreed upon those before you that you may become righteous' (2:183). Ramadan is not a diet month \u2014 it is a taqwa training camp: hunger teaches the body who is in charge.","Open the Fasting Guide","Read the essentials: who fasts, who is excused, and what breaks the fast.",u.rT,u.rT,"The Month of Training","Allah Wants Ease for You","The sick and the traveler may break the fast and make up the days later (2:184) \u2014 and 'Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship' (2:185). The exemption is not a loophole; it is the ruling itself showing mercy.",u.bC,u.bC,"The Mercy in the Exemption","The Fast of the Tongue","The Prophet \ufdfa said: \u201cWhoever does not give up forged speech and evil actions, Allah is not in need of his leaving his food and drink\u201d (Bukhari 1903). So Ramadan's hardest fast is not hunger; it is the tongue, the eyes and the hands. That is where taqwa is actually built.","The Fast of the Tongue, Tonight","Choose one habit of the tongue or the eyes to fast from until Maghrib, starting now.","Besides food and drink, what must the fasting person give up?","Besides food and drink, what must the fasting person give up (Bukhari 1903)?","Beyond the Empty Stomach","An Answer to a Call","'And proclaim to the people the Hajj [pilgrimage]; they will come to you on foot and on every lean camel' (22:27). Hajj is worship in motion \u2014 tawaf around the House, the walk of Hagar between Safa and Marwah, standing at Arafat where the religion was perfected (5:3).","Read the Hajj Overview Guide","Walk the sequence once in your mind: ihram, tawaf, sa'i, Arafat, Muzdalifah, Mina.",u.qd,u.qd,"The Journey of a Lifetime","Any Time of Year","Umrah is the smaller pilgrimage \u2014 tawaf, sa'i, cutting the hair \u2014 possible any time of year, completed in hours. If Hajj is the dissertation, Umrah is the visit that keeps the heart near the House.","Name the three acts that make up Umrah.","Name the three acts that make up Umrah.","Umrah \u2014 The Short Journey","Do Not Consume Unjustly","\u201cAnd do not consume one another's wealth unjustly\u201d (2:188). The Qur'an allows trade, but only \u201cbusiness by mutual consent\u201d (4:29). Your earnings are halal territory: honest work, honest measure, no riba (2:275-279 condemns it in the strongest words in the Qur'an). The barakah is in the honesty, not the amount.","Open the Zakat Guide","See the third pillar in action \u2014 nisab, the rates, and the giving that purifies wealth.","Which kind of trade does 4:29 allow?","Which kind of trade does 4:29 allow, in place of consuming one another's wealth unjustly?","Honest Wealth","Eat of the Good Things","'O mankind, eat from whatever is on earth [that is] lawful and good' (2:168). The default of food is permissibility; the exceptions are named \u2014 carrion, blood, pork, and what is dedicated to other than Allah (2:173), with necessity excusing (5:3). When in doubt about a particular food, ask a trusted scholar before you eat, and begin every meal with bismillah.",u.mU,u.mU,"The Halal Plate","No Mockery, No Suspicion, No Backbiting","'let not a people ridicule [another] people ... And do not spy or backbite each other' (49:11-12). Three commands guarding the social world. The test: would you say it with the person standing there? That question has ended more gossip than any lecture.","The Standing-There Test","For one day, run your speech through the test: would I say this with them here? Notice what changes.",u.xz,u.xz,"The Tongue's Territory","Lower the Wing","'And your Lord has decreed that you not worship except Him, and to parents, good treatment ... say not to them [so much as], uff ... And lower to them the wing of humility' (17:23-24). Here worship and kindness to parents are named side by side \u2014 with the word 'uff' forbidden.","One Act This Week","Do one unasked kindness for a parent this week \u2014 and if they are gone, give sadaqah for them or make dua at their grave.","What may you not say to your parents, not even so much?","What does 17:23 say you may not say to your parents, not even so much as this?","The Door of Parents","Love Is Placed, Not Found","'And of His signs is that He created for you from yourselves mates ... and He placed between you affection and mercy' (30:21). Allah did not say passion \u2014 He said affection (mawaddah) and mercy (rahmah). The home runs on mercy the way the body runs on blood.",u.hI,u.hI,"The Home as Mercy","The Strong One Controls at Anger","\u201cThe strong is not the one who overcomes the people by his strength, but the strong is the one who controls himself while in anger\u201d (Bukhari 6114). On the hardest day he had known, the Angel of the Mountains offered to let two mountains fall on those who had rejected him, and the Prophet \ufdfa said no: he hoped that Allah would bring from them children who would worship Allah alone (Bukhari 3231). Tonight's practice: let one thing go unavenged, unanswered, unreplied.","Tonight's Release","Before sleep, forgive one person in your heart \u2014 out loud or in silence. Then sleep on it.",u.d_,u.d_,"Forgiveness Before Sleep","Nothing Is Lost","'Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it' (99:7-8). Every act is recorded and will be shown \u2014 the terrifying mercy of perfect justice. Nothing you did in secret is lost, good or bad.",u.qP,u.qP,"The Weight of an Atom","What Allah Prepared for Those Near Him","'reclining therein on adorned couches ... Upon the inhabitants will be green garments of fine silk and brocade. And they will be adorned with bracelets of silver' (76:12-21). The Qur'an describes the reward so your heart can want it \u2014 wanting Jannah is half the journey to it.","Read a Jannah Story Tonight","Open the Prophets or Tales collection and read one description of the reward before sleep.",u.AL,u.AL,"Gardens Prepared","The Appointment No One Misses","'And spend from what We have provided you before death approaches one of you' (63:10) \u2014 and no soul is delayed when its time comes (63:11). The Hereafter unit does not end in fear. The Prophet \ufdfa taught that when a person dies their deeds stop, except three: ongoing charity (sadaqah jariyah), beneficial knowledge, and a righteous child who prays for them (Muslim 1631).","Plant One Thing That Outlives You","Name one ongoing charity you can start this month \u2014 even small: a recurring gift, a taught skill, a shared dua.",u.CN,u.CN,"Every Soul Will Taste Death","Du'a & Adhkar School","The daily words of remembrance \u2014 what they mean, when to say them, and where they come from.","Arabic Language School","The language of the Qur\u2019an itself \u2014 words, sentences, and grammar, taught from Qur\u2019anic examples.","Hifz School","Memorize the Quran with the sabaq, sabqi, manzil cycle \u2014 your pace, your compass, never your judge.","Aqeedah School","Who Allah is, what He sent, and why it changes a life \u2014 taught from the Quran itself.","Hadith School","Imam an-Nawawi\u2019s Forty, taught one hadith at a time \u2014 text, meaning, and the character it builds.","Seerah School","The life of the Prophet (peace be upon him) era by era \u2014 every chapter opens the real story.","History School","The centuries after the Prophet \u2014 the four caliphs, the scholars, and the ages they carried.","Stories School","The library\u2019s stories as a moral curriculum \u2014 patience, courage, mercy, and gratitude, each with a family question.","Character School","The heart\u2019s traits \u2014 sincerity, patience, gratitude, and their enemies \u2014 each with one practice for today.","Family Life School","Marriage, children, and the home as a place of worship \u2014 mercy between you, the trust of children.","Youth School","Identity, the phone, friends, and money \u2014 the tests of a generation, with one practice each.","Women\u2019s School","The women of the Quran and the Prophet\u2019s household \u2014 iman that built, scholarship that taught, standing that changed history.","Transactions School","Halal earnings, riba, zakat in practice, and the barakah of honest work.","End of Life School","The will, the janazah, the last words \u2014 preparing to meet Allah with dignity and hope.","Dawah School","How to carry the message with wisdom \u2014 the Makkan method, answers to the hard questions, the caller\u2019s character.","Health & Ruqyah School","The body as an amanah \u2014 halal food, sleep, the Quran as medicine, the heart\u2019s health.","Hisn al-Muslim","The Fortress of the Muslim \u2014 every authentic dua and dhikr, categorized for the moment you are in.","Hajj & Umrah Pack","The journey in order \u2014 intention, the rites, the days \u2014 opening the real guides at every station.","Ramadan Mode","The month of taqwa \u2014 pillars, daily rhythm, and the doors of suhoor, iftar, and taraweeh.","Verse Cards","Shareable Quran and hadith cards \u2014 framed in gold, one tap to send down any road a message can travel.","Q&A Bank","Curated questions with sourced answers \u2014 the starting points every Muslim needs.","As-salamu alaykum \u2014 peace be upon you \u2014 is a Quranic formula: the Prophet \ufdfa is told to greet the believers who come to him with it (6:54), and the angels greet the people of Paradise with 'peace be upon you for what you patiently endured' (13:24). The reply mirrors it. Every greeting is Quranic Arabic.","Say the greeting and its reply, then tell someone what 6:54 and 13:24 say.","The Greeting Is a Quranic Sentence","Ab (father), umm (mother), ibn/bint (son/daughter) \u2014 the words that carry the Quran's family passages: Yusuf and his father (12:4), a mother who carries her child (46:15), Luqman and his son (31:13), Maryam ibnat 'Imran (66:12). Learn these four and the family words in many verses will already be familiar.","Name the four family words and one verse each appears in.","Family Words You Already Own",u.xa,"Give three words you know with al- and three without.","The Definite Article: Al-","Allah is the proper Name; rabb is the noun (Lord, Nurturer). In the Quran rabb is almost always joined to what it governs \u2014 rabbi al-'alamin, rabbuna, rabbuka \u2014 rather than standing alone with al-.","See it in Al-Fatiha \u2014 open the reader and read 1:2.","Open the reader, find Al-Fatiha, and read 1:2 slowly.","Allah Is the Name, Rabb Is the Word","First Words, Real Words","Greetings, family, and the definite article \u2014 from the Quran",u.y5,"Recite it in the reader \u2014 tap any verse to hear it.","Open the reader and tap a verse to hear it recited.","Al-Fatiha, Word by Word","Iyyaka na'budu \u2014 You alone we worship. Iyyaka (You) is placed before the verb, which is what gives the sentence its 'alone'; na'budu is the present-tense verb, and the na- means 'we'. Salah is a daily Arabic lesson the body never forgets.","Point to iyyaka and na'budu in the mushaf the next time you pray.","The Formula You Say 17 Times a Day","And recite the Quran with measured recitation (73:4). Slow enough to hear each letter. Arabic learned slowly stays; Arabic rushed evaporates.",u.lY,"Slow Is the Standard","Reading Whole Verses","Al-Fatiha word by word, and the pacing of recitation","Arabic Language","The language of the Quran, taught from its own words","'The Most Merciful Taught the Qur'an' (55:1\u20132). Before any rule, the Quran opens its knowledge of Allah with a mercy that teaches. Begin here.","What does 55:1\u20132 teach about how Allah introduces Himself?","The Most Merciful Taught the Book","'Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of [all] existence. Neither drowsiness overtakes Him nor sleep' (2:255). Ayat al-Kursi \u2014 many say it after every prayer; now you know what it says.","Recite Ayat al-Kursi and name the two attributes that describe His wakefulness.","No Slumber, No Sleep","'In the name of Allah, the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful' (1:1). Every surah but one opens with mercy named twice. The name you say most is the Merciful.","Why is mercy named twice in the basmala \u2014 what might the two mercies be?","The Attribute We Say Most","'And to Allah belong the best names, so invoke Him by them' (7:180). The 99 Names are self-descriptions, each one an answer to a human need.","Meet them in the memory deck \u2014 open the 99 Names.","Open the 99 Names deck and read the first few.","His Are the Most Beautiful Names","Who Is Allah","The names and attributes, from the Quran itself","'Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam' (3:19). Every nation received the same call: worship Allah and avoid false gods (16:36). The chain you belong to is as old as Adam.","What is the one message every messenger brought?","Not a New God \u2014 the Same Call","'a guidance for those conscious of Allah - Who believe in the unseen' (2:2-3). Faith begins where sight ends \u2014 angels, the Last Day, the reward.","Name three things a believer believes in that cannot be seen.","The Unseen Is Not Unheard","'We certainly sent into every nation a messenger' (16:36). Ibrahim argued with a star; Musa stood before a sea; Isa healed by Allah's leave; Muhammad sealed the chain.","Walk their stories \u2014 open the Prophets collection.","Open the Stories shelves and read one story of a prophet.","A Messenger to Every Nation","What He Sent","The one message, the unseen, the messengers","'He is with you wherever you are' (57:4). 'We are closer to him than his jugular vein' (50:16). 'Fear not. Indeed, I am with you both; I hear and I see' (20:46). You are never actually alone.","Which of the three 'with you' verses speaks to your season right now?","He Is With You \u2014 the Three Ways","'And the heaven He raised and imposed the balance, that you not transgress within the balance' (55:7-8). Justice is built into creation itself.","Where in your life does the balance need adjusting?","The Balance","Aqeedah is not an exam to pass; it is a Person to know. The more beautiful your picture of Him, the braver your worship becomes.","Complete the sentence: 'When I remember that Allah is ___, I feel ___ differently.'","A Creed You Can Carry","Why It Matters","The change that knowing Allah makes in a life","Aqeedah","Who Allah is, what He sent, and why it changes a life","The teaching","Actions are only by intentions (Bukhari 1). The same prayer can be worship or theater depending on the why.","Practice",u.jv,"Sincerity: the reason behind the deed","The teaching","Allah is with the patient (2:153). Ya'qub said 'I only complain of my suffering and my grief to Allah' (12:86).","Practice",u.kL,"Patience: holding on with Allah","The teaching","If you are grateful, I will surely increase you (14:7).","Practice",u.iy,"Gratitude: the promise of increase","The teaching","Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise (Bukhari 6094).","Practice",u.ot,"Truthfulness: the road and the story of Kab","The Weight You Carry","Sincerity, patience, gratitude, truthfulness","The teaching","The strong is not the wrestler; the strong is the one who controls himself at anger (Bukhari 6114).","Practice","Next time anger rises: sit down and stay silent for ninety seconds.","Anger: control and refuge","The teaching","Envy eats good deeds as fire eats dry wood \u2014 a report graded weak, so hold it as a reminder (Abu Dawud 4903, weak per al-Albani). The cure: pray for the one who has it.","Practice",u.j1,"Envy: the second look","The teaching","No one with a mustard seed's weight of pride in his heart enters Paradise (Muslim 91).","Practice",u.ty,"Arrogance: the false height","The teaching","Say: O My servants who have transgressed, do not despair of the mercy of Allah (39:53).","Practice",u.rJ,"Despair: the door that is open","The Heart's Enemies","Anger, envy, arrogance, despair","The teaching","Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent (Bukhari 6018).","Practice","Run today's speech through one filter: would I say it with the person standing here?","The tongue: your daily ledger","The teaching","Allah loves the doers of good \u2014 those who spend in ease and hardship, who restrain their anger, and who pardon people (3:134).","Practice",u.A9,"Forgiveness: releasing the debt","The teaching","The Prophet \ufdfa was in the service of his family (Bukhari 676).","Practice",u.zl,"Kindness: the Prophet at home","The teaching","The believers are like one body \u2014 if the eye aches the whole body aches (Bukhari 6011).","Practice",u.ux,"Brotherhood: the whole body","The Social Heart","Tongue, forgiveness, kindness, brotherhood","Character","The heart's traits \u2014 what builds them, what attacks them","Why Marriage at All","Marriage is described with three words: sukun (tranquility), mawaddah (affection), and rahmah (mercy) (30:21). The house runs on mercy the way the body runs on blood.","Practice",u.t3,"Why Marriage at All","The Best of You","The best of you is the one who is best to his wife (Tirmidhi 3895, hasan per Darussalam, sahih per al-Albani). The measure of a Muslim is not the masjid face; it is the kitchen face.","Practice",u.e5,"The Best of You","Mercy Between You","Allah describes spouses as garments for one another (2:187) \u2014 covering faults, providing warmth. The garment does not criticize the body it covers.","Practice",u.AF,"Mercy Between You","Marriage \u2014 A Solemn Covenant","Calm, affection and mercy at home","The First Teacher","Your mother carries you in weakness upon weakness (31:14) \u2014 and the Prophet said she most deserves good company three times before your father (Bukhari 5971).","Practice",u.CG,"The First Teacher","Teaching the Prayer","Command your children to pray at seven and discipline them about it at ten, and separate their beds (Abu Dawud 495, hasan sahih per al-Albani). Before seven the prayer is invited, not enforced.","Practice",u.aJ,"Teaching the Prayer","Mercy, Not Severity","Allah is Merciful and loves mercy in all things (Bukhari 6927). The Prophet never struck a servant or a woman, and never struck anything with his hand except in battle (Muslim 2328).","Practice",u.v1,"Mercy, Not Severity","The Best Provision","A parent gives more than food and school fees: manners, faith and du'a. Luqman taught his son to worship Allah alone and to pray (31:13, 31:17).","Practice",u.gl,"The Best Provision","Children \u2014 The Trust","Your children are an amanah","Serving the Family","Aisha was asked what the Prophet did at home. She said: he was in the service of his family (Bukhari 676). He mended his clothes, milked the goat, swept.","Practice",u.yN,"Serving the Family","The Family That Prays","The Prophet said the one who remembers his Lord and the one who does not are like the living and the dead (Bukhari 6407). Let the home be a place of dhikr.","Practice",u.yK,"The Family That Prays","Forgiveness in the House","The Prophet said no one forgives another except that Allah increases his honor (Muslim 2588). The house needs this most.","Practice",u.vD,"Forgiveness in the House","The Home as Worship","The house is not a pause between acts of worship","Family Life","Marriage, children, and the home as worship","The Honor You Were Born With","Allah says He honored the children of Adam (17:70). The verdict on your worth was issued by the One who made you.","Practice",u.oT,"The Honor You Were Born With","Chosen \u2014 Adam's Answer","When Allah announced the khilafah, the angels asked about one who sheds blood; He said: I know that which you do not know (2:30). You were created with a purpose the angels could not see.","Practice","Name one thing you are good at that could serve the ummah \u2014 even small. That is the 'which you do not know.'","Chosen \u2014 Adam's Answer","Carrying the Faith Forward","The Prophet said the best generation is his, then the next, then the next (Bukhari 2652). He also called the believers who come later his brothers (Muslim 249). The faith is yours to learn and carry.","Practice","Pick one sunnah you can practice this week that your friends will notice \u2014 and let them ask about it.","Carrying the Faith Forward","Identity \u2014 Who You Are","The honor you were born with","The Scroll That Eats the Hour","The five prayers are five anchors; the feed is a current that pulls you under. Screens can make strangers of us at our own dinner tables.","Practice",u.lg,"The Scroll That Eats the Hour","The Feed Is Not Real","You are comparing your inside to everyone else's outside. The Prophet said Allah does not look at your appearances or wealth but at your hearts and deeds (Muslim 2564), not likes.","Practice",u.kx,"The Feed Is Not Real","Guarding the Gaze","Tell the believing men to lower their gaze and guard their chastity (24:30) \u2014 and the believing women likewise (24:31). The screen made the gaze the easiest sin; the verse did not change.","Practice",u.oy,"Guarding the Gaze","The Phone \u2014 Your 21st Century Companion","The scroll that eats the hour","Choose Your Company","A person is upon the religion of his friend (Tirmidhi 2378, hasan per Darussalam). Choose the friend your future self will thank you for.","Practice",u.Ex,"Choose Your Company","Halal Money \u2014 Even the Penny","The Prophet said: leave that which makes you doubt for that which does not (Tirmidhi 2518, sahih per Darussalam). The barakah is in the clean dirham, even when the unclean one is bigger.","Practice",u.bo,"Halal Money \u2014 Even the Penny","Seven Under the Shade","Seven whom Allah will shade \u2014 among them a youth who grew up in the worship of Allah (Bukhari 660). Your energy and memory are capital no billionaire can buy back.","Practice","Spend thirty minutes this week on one act of worship you cannot do when you are older \u2014 memorization, night prayer, learning Arabic.","Seven Under the Shade","Friends & Money","The two currencies of youth","Youth",u.Er,"Khadijah \u2014 The First Believer","The first person to believe was a woman \u2014 a merchant who financed the mission. When the Prophet came down from Hira trembling, she wrapped him and said: Allah will never disgrace you.","Practice","Who believed in you before anyone else? Thank them this week \u2014 by name.","Khadijah: the first to stand with him","Asiya \u2014 The Palace of Pharaoh","She lived in the tyrant's house and was heartbroken in it \u2014 and Allah showed her her house in Paradise (66:11). Sometimes the palace is the test, not the prize.","Practice",u.Au,"Asiya: faith in the tyrant\u2019s house","Maryam \u2014 The Palm Tree","Alone, in labor, accused \u2014 and the angels spoke to her (19:16-33). Allah named a surah after a woman: surah 19, Maryam.","Practice",u.mR,"Maryam: the palm tree","Hagar \u2014 She Ran Seven Times","Alone in a barren valley with a crying child \u2014 and her trust that He will not waste them became the walk between Safa and Marwah (2:158). Her tawakkul built a rite.","Practice",u.ix,"Hajar: she ran seven times","Iman That Built","The first believers, the first martyrs","Aisha \u2014 The Scholar of Scholars","The companions asked her about inheritance, medicine, poetry. Her student Urwa said he had never seen anyone more knowledgeable in fiqh, medicine, or poetry.","Practice",u.R,"Aisha: the slander and the verdict","Fatima \u2014 The Brightest House","The Prophet asked her whether she would be pleased to be the chief of the women of Paradise (Bukhari 3624) \u2014 and she complained of the hardship of grinding at the hand mill and went to ask for a servant (Bukhari 3113). The highest rank and the grinding stone in the same hands.","Practice",u.aQ,"Fatima: a part of him","Hafsa \u2014 The Keeper of the Book","After the Prophet's passing, the first written Quran was kept with Hafsa \u2014 the ummah's first librarian. Uthman's standard copies were made from her sheets.","Practice","Guard one thing of value this week \u2014 a book, a memory, a person's secret.","Hafsa: keeper of the pages","Umm Ayman \u2014 The One They Forgot to List","She raised the Prophet after his parents died \u2014 and he called her 'my mother after my mother.' The barakah often lives with the person no one mentions.","Practice",u.tJ,"Umm Ayman: the one who raised him","Scholarship That Taught","The first scholars were the women of the Prophet's house","Sumayyah \u2014 The First to Give Everything","The first martyr of Islam was a slave woman. Abu Jahl's spear could not make her curse the Prophet \u2014 so she became the ummah's first lesson in standing.","Practice",u.eD,"Sumayyah: patience when few","Nusaybah \u2014 Umm Ammarah","At Uhud, when the line broke and men fled, she stood between the Prophet and the swords \u2014 shielding him with her body until she was cut. The Prophet said: wherever I turned, she was there.","Practice",u.Ae,"Nusaybah and the women of Uhud","Khawlah \u2014 Whose Complaint Allah Heard","Her husband had pronounced zihar against her. She brought her complaint to the Prophet \ufdfa and to Allah \u2014 and Allah heard her: 'Certainly has Allah heard the speech of the one who argues with you concerning her husband and directs her complaint to Allah' (58:1). Scholars of tafsir report this verse was revealed about Khawlah, and the ruling that follows is in 58:2-4. Bringing your grievance to Allah is never wasted.","Practice",u.bG,"Khawlah: Allah heard her","Asma \u2014 She Who Carried the Food","During the Hijrah, Asma bint Abi Bakr prepared provisions for the Prophet \ufdfa and her father and tore her waist-belt in two to tie them, and is remembered as Dhat an-Nitaqayn, the one of the two belts (reported in the hadith and seerah sources). The cave of the Hijrah is itself mentioned in 9:40. The logistics of a journey on one woman's belt.","Practice","What are you carrying for someone else's journey? Keep carrying it.","Asma: two belts and a kind heart","Umm Salama \u2014 The Dua of the Afflicted","When her husband Abu Salama died she said the dua of the afflicted \u2014 'Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return' (2:156) \u2014 and Allah gave her something better, marriage to the Prophet \ufdfa (Muslim 918). Separately, women's questions about why the Qur'an seemed to address men are reported to have preceded 33:35 (Tirmidhi 3211, hasan per Darussalam, from Umm Umarah, hasan).","Practice",u.qe,"Umm Salama: words in grief, advice in a crisis","Standing That Changed History","When the line broke, the women held it","Zaynab \u2014 Generosity That Hurt","She gave so much the Prophet told her to keep something for herself \u2014 and she answered that Allah would replace it. The wife who out-gave the household.","Practice",u.aI,"Zaynab bint Jahsh: the long hand",u.ib,"Taken in battle, she asked for her freedom; he offered marriage. Her mahr freed her whole clan. The captivity narrative ended in a wedding that freed a hundred families.","Practice","Who is a captive of circumstance \u2014 and what could you free them from this month?","Juwayriyya: freedom and four words","Safiyya \u2014 The Woman Who Answered","Mocked for her Jewish ancestry, she answered: 'Aaron is my father, Moses my uncle, and Muhammad my husband.' The answer that silenced the mockers.","Practice",u.rU,"Safiyya: care and closing the door on doubt","Bilqis \u2014 The Queen Who Knew a Letter","She ruled a kingdom, and a letter from Sulayman rearranged her throne. She kept her crown and found her Lord. The Qur'an does not name her; it describes a woman ruling them (27:23), and the name Bilqis comes from later tradition.","Practice","What letter has reached you that deserves an answer like Bilqis's?","The queen of Sheba: consult and submit","The Wives \u2014 Mothers of the Believers","The teachers of a generation","Women in the Deen","Iman, scholarship, standing, and the mothers of the believers","Do Not Consume Unjustly","And do not consume one another's wealth unjustly, nor use it to bribe judges (2:188). Even when the trade is by mutual consent, the unjust line can still be crossed.","Practice",u.up,"Do Not Consume Unjustly","The Birds Leave Hungry","The Prophet said: if you relied upon Allah as He deserves, He would provide you as He provides the birds \u2014 they leave hungry and return full (Tirmidhi 2344, hasan per Darussalam).","Practice",u.yz,"The Birds Leave Hungry","The Honest Measure","Woe to the defrauders (83:1-3). The Prophet found the seller had watered the grain \u2014 he said: the one who cheats is not one of us (Muslim 102).","Practice",u.l8,"The Honest Measure","Honest Work Over Easy Wealth","The Prophet said: Allah loves a servant who is pious, independent, and hidden (Muslim 2965). The hand that works is raised in dua.","Practice",u.E2,"Honest Work Over Easy Wealth","Halal Earnings","The barakah is in the honesty, not the amount","What Riba Actually Is","Riba is stipulated increase on a loan \u2014 interest, usury. Allah permitted trade and forbidden riba (2:275). A loan is a trust, not a product.","Practice","Check one of your financial products: is any charge stipulated on the loan itself? Ask a scholar about it.","What Riba Actually Is","Interest in Everyday Life","Those who consume riba will rise like one whom Satan has struck into madness, and they are warned of the Fire (2:275); Allah destroys riba and gives increase to charity (2:276). Leaving it is a discipline, taken one step at a time.","Practice","Name one riba-based habit (a card balance carried, a BNPL plan). Set an exit date \u2014 even a year away \u2014 and write it down.","Interest in Everyday Life","Leaving Riba With Dignity","Allah commands: give up what remains of riba (2:278); if you repent you keep your principal, wronging no one and wronged by no one (2:279). And if a debtor is in hardship, grant respite until ease \u2014 forgiving the debt is better still (2:280). The exit is a declaration of which side of the war you are on.","Practice",u.va,"Leaving Riba With Dignity","Riba \u2014 The War You Declared","Allah declares war on the riba-taker (2:278-279)","Zakat on Savings","Zakat is due on zakatable wealth held above the nisab for one lunar year, at 2.5%. The recipients are named in one verse (9:60).","Practice",u.AC,"Zakat on Savings","Debt and the Door","The Prophet said: whoever takes people's wealth intending to repay it, Allah will repay it for him (Bukhari 2387). Debt is a weight \u2014 but the weight has a door.","Practice",u.mT,"Debt and the Door","Barakah, Not Just More","Barakah is being satisfied with what you took honestly (Bukhari 1472). Faith helps, and so does seeing a doctor or counsellor when you are worn out.","Practice",u.xW,"Barakah, Not Just More","Zakat in Practice & Wealth That Purifies","The third pillar in the modern wallet","Transactions","Halal earnings, riba, zakat in practice, and the barakah of honest work","Every Soul Will Taste It","Every soul will taste death, and only on the Day of Judgment will you be paid in full (3:185). The verse is not a threat; it is the calendar.","Practice",u.h6,"Every soul will taste it","The Will \u2014 Writing It Is a Sunna","The Prophet said: it is not right for a Muslim who has something to bequeath to sleep two nights without having his will written (Bukhari 2738).","Practice","Draft your will this month \u2014 even a page: debts, guardianship, the small bequests.","The will: write it, and write it well","The Estate \u2014 Fair Before the End","Allah commands you concerning your children: the male receives the share of two females (4:11). The shares are Allah's math, not the family's negotiation.","Practice",u.Al,"The estate: Allah\u2019s shares","Plant What Outlives You","When a person dies, their deeds end except three: ongoing charity, knowledge that benefits, and a righteous child who prays for them (Muslim 1631).","Practice",u.zq,"Plant what outlives you","Preparing Before the Hour","Remember often the destroyer of pleasures (Tirmidhi 2307, hasan per Darussalam)","La Ilaha Illa Allah \u2014 the Last Word","Whoever's last words are la ilaha illa Allah enters Paradise (Abu Dawud 3116, sahih per al-Albani). Prompt your dying to say it, gently, without burden.","Practice",u.q8,"La ilaha illa Allah: the last word","The Prayer Over the Dead","The janazah prayer is offered standing, without bowing or prostration.","Practice",u.fT,"The funeral prayer: no bowing, no prostration","Grieving Is Allowed","The Prophet wept at his son's death and said: the eyes weep and the heart grieves, and we say only what pleases our Lord (Bukhari 1303). Tears are not weakness.","Practice",u.dX,"Grief and comfort: what to say and do","The Final Days","How the believer meets the end","The Grave Is a Garden","The Prophet said the grave is either a garden from the gardens of Paradise or a pit from the pits of Fire \u2014 a report in Tirmidhi 2460, weak per Darussalam, so hold it as a reminder, not a ruling. What you send ahead matters either way.","Practice",u.kw,"The grave: the first stop","The Meeting You Are Walking Toward","Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him (Bukhari 6507; Muslim 2684). The companions lived with this hadith the way travelers live with a map.","Practice",u.hh,"Meeting Allah: hope and fear","Hope Forward","The school ends where the grave begins: with light","End of Life","The will, the janazah, the last words \u2014 preparing with dignity","Invite to the Oneness First","When the Prophet sent Mus'ab to Madinah, he did not send rulings \u2014 he sent the shahada. The first question is never 'what about hijab' \u2014 it is 'who is Allah, and what does He ask of you?'","Practice","In your next conversation about Islam, begin with Allah's mercy and oneness \u2014 not the rules. Let the heart open before the law arrives.","Invite to the Oneness First","Wisdom Is Knowing the Person","Call to the way of your Lord with wisdom and good instruction, and argue with them in the best way (16:125). The message is one; the door is tailored.","Practice",u.js,"Wisdom Is Knowing the Person","The Taif Standard","When the people of Taif stoned him until his shoes filled with blood, the angel offered to crush the city. The Prophet said: no \u2014 perhaps Allah will bring forth from them those who will worship Him alone (Bukhari 3231).","Practice","When someone mocks your faith this week, respond with the Taif standard \u2014 no counter-mockery. Deliver the mercy, release the result.","The Taif Standard","Your Life Is the Loudest Sermon","The Prophet was called al-Amin \u2014 the trustworthy \u2014 before he was called a prophet. His character opened the door his words then walked through.","Practice","Audit one relationship: does your character open the door or close it? Repair the one that closes it.","Your Life Is the Loudest Sermon","The Method","Thirteen years in Makkah teaching one family, then one tribe, then a city","Why Do Bad Things Happen?","Do not say about anything 'I will do that tomorrow' without adding 'if Allah wills' (18:23-24). And: perhaps you dislike a thing and it is good for you (2:216). The answer is trust that the Author sees the whole book.","Practice",u.kK,"Why Do Bad Things Happen?","Islam Is Too Strict","Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship (2:185). And: fear Allah as much as you are able (64:16). The deen has a floor and a ceiling; show the floor first.","Practice","Describe Islam by its mercy (the door of repentance, the ease in hardship) before its boundaries.","Islam Is Too Strict","The Quran Was Written by a Man","The Qur'an challenges those who doubt it: bring ten surahs like it (11:13), or just one surah like it (10:38; 2:23). The challenge stands 1400 years later.","Practice",u.cX,"The Quran Was Written by a Man","I Have Done Too Much Wrong","Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah; indeed, Allah forgives all sins (39:53). The verse for the one who thinks they are too far gone.","Practice","When someone confesses a sin, respond with 39:53 before any advice. The verse first, always.","I Have Done Too Much Wrong","The Answers","The Quran itself teaches how to answer","Gentleness Does Not Water Down the Truth","Gentleness is not found in anything except that it adds beauty to it (Muslim 2594). Musa was sent to Pharaoh \u2014 and still told: speak to him mildly (20:44).","Practice",u.v2,"Gentleness Does Not Water Down the Truth","Knowledge Before Speech","Say: my Lord has only forbidden what is apparent of immorality and what is concealed (7:33). A half-answer delivered with confidence closes more doors than silence. When you do not know, say: I will find out.","Practice","When asked something you do not know, practice: 'That is a beautiful question \u2014 let me find out and come back to you.'","Knowledge Before Speech","Release the Result","You are not over them a controller (88:22). Your job is to deliver clearly, kindly, honestly; the heart that opens is Allah's to open.","Practice",u.Ew,"Release the Result","The Caller's Character","The message is carried by the messenger","Dawah",u.AA,"Eat of the Good Things","O people, eat from the earth what is lawful and good, and do not follow the footsteps of Shaytan (2:168). The halal plate is an invitation to eat well, eat clean, and eat with gratitude.","Practice",u.cd,"Eat of the good things","The Third of the Stomach","The son of Adam does not fill any vessel worse than his stomach \u2014 a few morsels for his back to stand straight; if he must fill it, a third for food, a third for drink, a third for breath (Tirmidhi 2380, sahih per Darussalam).","Practice",u.aN,"The third of the stomach","Sleep Is Worship's Fuel","When one of you goes to bed, let him brush his hand over his bed \u2014 for he does not know what came upon it after him \u2014 then say: in Your name, my Lord, I lay down my side (Bukhari 6320). Sleep entered the sunna.","Practice",u.Dl,"Sleep: a right of your body","Moderation in All Things","The Prophet said: the religion is ease (Bukhari 39). He fasted but did not fast continuously; he prayed but he slept; he worked but he rested. Extremism in worship is a debt the body will collect.","Practice",u.iC,"Moderation in all things","The Body as an Amanah","Your body is a trust \u2014 you did not build it, you were lent it","The Prophet's Own Ruqyah","The Prophet \ufdfa taught someone in pain to place a hand on the spot that hurts, say bismillah three times, then say seven times: I seek refuge in Allah's might and power from the evil of what I feel and fear (Muslim 2202).","Practice",u.sk,"The Prophet\u2019s own ruqyah","The Evil Eye Is Real \u2014 and Curable","The evil eye is real, and if anything were to overtake the divine decree, it would be the evil eye (Muslim 2188). The cure: the mu'awwidhat (the last three surahs) recited over the afflicted.","Practice","When you admire something \u2014 your child, your home \u2014 say mashallah, la quwwata illa billah. Guard the blessing by naming its Owner.","The evil eye: real, and curable","When Medicine and Faith Meet","Allah did not send down a disease without sending down its cure (Bukhari 5678). Use the medicine \u2014 the ruqyah does not cancel the doctor; the doctor does not cancel the ruqyah.","Practice",u.dk,"Medicine and faith together","Ruqyah \u2014 the Quran as Medicine","We send down of the Quran that which is healing and mercy (17:82)","The Day of the Heart's Surgery","The day when neither wealth nor children will avail, except one who comes to Allah with a sound heart (26:88-89). The sound heart is the only luggage that boards.","Practice",u.cW,"The sound heart","Dhikr Is the Heart's Food","Those who remember Allah standing, sitting, and on their sides (3:191). The heart without dhikr is the body without food \u2014 it does not die loudly; it just grows numb.","Practice",u.lM,"Dhikr: food for the heart","The Heart's Health","The body's final organ is the heart","Health & Ruqyah","The body as an amanah, the Quran as medicine, the heart's health","A Revelation, Not a Book First","The Quran arrived as sound before paper: Jibril brought it over twenty-three years, and the first word was Iqra \u2014 read (96:1).","Practice","Read one verse aloud today \u2014 hear it as the first listeners heard it.","A Revelation, Not a Book First","Guarded, Word by Word","'Indeed, it is We who sent down the Qur'an and indeed, We will be its guardian' (15:9). The protection is of the text itself \u2014 memorized by millions, letter by letter.","Practice","Recite one verse you know from memory \u2014 you are part of the guarding.","Guarded, Word by Word","Why Arabic","'We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an that you might understand' (12:2). The language is not a barrier \u2014 it is the vessel of the meaning.","Practice","Learn one Arabic word from a verse you love \u2014 just one, this week.","Why Arabic","How the Quran Came","A revelation, not a book first","Translation Is a Bridge","Every translation is an interpretation wearing the translator's glasses. Read with gratitude and a light grip \u2014 when a word carries your heart, check the Arabic.","Practice","Find one verse where the translation surprised you \u2014 look up the Arabic word behind it.","Translation Is a Bridge","Recite With Measured Beauty","'and recite the Qur'an with measured recitation' (73:4). Slow enough to hear yourself. Understanding grows in the pause between verses.","Practice",u.lY,"Recite With Measured Beauty","None Touch It Except the Purified","'None touch it except the purified' (56:79). Begin with wudu, begin with ta'awwudh, begin with His name.","Practice","Make wudu before your next Quran reading \u2014 even a short one.","None Touch It Except the Purified","Reading With Meaning","Translation is a bridge, not the land","A Fixed Portion, However Small","The most beloved deeds to Allah are the most consistent, even if small (Bukhari 6464). A standard mushaf has 604 pages, so one page a day finishes the Quran in about twenty months.","Practice","Set a daily portion \u2014 even half a page \u2014 and protect it for one week.","A Fixed Portion, However Small","Open","'And We send down of the Qur'an that which is healing and mercy for the believers' (17:82). Find the verse that answers your season.","Healing and Mercy","The Abandoned Qur'an","On the Day, the Messenger \ufdfa will say: 'O my Lord, indeed my people have taken this Qur'an as [a thing] abandoned' (25:30). Abandonment includes opening it and hearing nothing.","Practice","Read one verse today as if it were addressed to you. It is.","The Abandoned Qur'an","The Quran in a Day","A fixed portion, however small","Understanding the Quran","How it came, how to read it, how it lives in a day","The Three Lanes","Every day has three lanes: sabaq (new memorization), sabqi (recent revision of the last week), and manzil (long-range revision of older sections). The cycle keeps the whole Quran alive, not just the newest part.","Practice","Name your three lanes for today \u2014 what is new, what is recent, what is old?","The Three Lanes","Start Where You Pray","Begin with the surahs you already pray. The mushaf you recite daily is the easiest to memorize.","Practice","Pick the surah you pray most \u2014 start there this week.","Start Where You Pray","Open","The Hifz planner projects your completion date and builds your daily lanes. A teacher sets your actual pace; the planner keeps you honest.","Set Your Pace","Beginning the Memorization","The sabaq, sabqi, manzil cycle","Recent Revision","Sabqi revises the last week of memorization. Without it, the newest memorization evaporates within days. The revision is not optional \u2014 it is the memorization.","Practice","Recite yesterday's sabaq before today's new memorization \u2014 always.","Recent Revision","Long-Range Revision","Manzil revises one completed section daily, cycling through the whole Quran. The goal is not to re-memorize but to keep the old memorization warm.","Practice","Set a manzil section for this week \u2014 one juz or one surah, cycled daily.","Long-Range Revision","The Listening Ear","Recite to a checker \u2014 a teacher, a family member, or your own recording played back. The ear catches what the tongue misses.","Practice","Record yourself reciting today's sabaq \u2014 then listen for the errors.","The Listening Ear","Keeping What You Memorize","Revision is the heart of memorization","Hifz","Memorize with the sabaq, sabqi, manzil cycle","Al-Wasia Academy of Sacred Knowledge","The schools","Reviews due","Learning track","Child","Teen","Adult","Parent","Changes what this page shows. On the Child track, other tracks and the other schools open only with a grown-up\u2019s PIN.","Where would you like to begin?","I\u2019m new to Islam","A gentle first lesson, then one step at a time.","It\u2019s for my child","Wasia teaches the Arabic letters, one at a time.","I\u2019m coming back","Take me to the Academy.","You can change this at any time.","Wasia\u2019s School","Letters with Wasia","Let\u2019s meet our first letter","Our next letter","All the letters are done. Well done!","lessons done","to look at again","More schools, with a grown-up","These schools are for older learners. A grown-up enters their PIN to open them.","The Family Wing","See your children\u2019s lessons and exams, set reminders, and control the AI setting.","words due","Lessons to revisit","Coming soon \u2014 insha\u2019Allah","Continue where you left off","Start here","Next lesson","Begin the Path","Today","lessons completed","words reviewed","ayat listened","A verse for the learner","Translation: Saheeh International (interim) \u2014 The Clear Quran\xae preferred, license pending","Your turn","Before moving on, do it or say it back in your own words \u2014 out loud or in your heart.","Done, continue","Show me again","WATCH AND FOLLOW","3D instructor \u2014 plays in the app with the avatar player","Next","Back","Done","Open","Try once more","Recall check","Made from this lesson\u2019s own words. It checks that you remember what the lesson said \u2014 it is not a ruling and does not make the lesson more or less correct.","Check your understanding","Alhamdulillah \u2014 every answer correct.","Let\u2019s look at it once more, gently.","Check my answers","Answer every question, then check.","One more look","You will see these once more. Nothing is lost if you miss them again.","The answer","PUT IN ORDER","The recording could not be played right now.","Back to the question","What you can now do","That is the last question.","Check the order","CITED IN THIS LESSON","You will see this question once more.","DO IT FOR REAL","You can come back to this lesson afterwards.","Finish","part(s) of this lesson are marked for a scholar to review.","Answer to go on. A wrong answer shows you why, and you can look at the step again.","Hear it","HOW TO","LISTEN AND REPEAT","Listen and repeat","Listen, then say it aloud","MATCH","All matched.","COMMON MISTAKES","Next question","There is no recording of this line yet. Say it slowly, a few words at a time.","Not quite.","RECAP","Reciter","STEPS TO PLACE","This lesson will come back for a short review in a day or so.","Right.","SAY IT","WHAT WOULD YOU DO?","WHERE THE SCHOOLS DIFFER","These are differences between scholars of the four schools, not mistakes.","Show me that step","sources","The Arabic is copied letter for letter from the Qur\u2019an text in this app or from the hadith it cites. The transliterations, the meanings of phrases and the explanations are the app\u2019s own words and have not yet been reviewed by a scholar. Where the schools differ, the lesson says so.","Stop","STORY","Tap a placed step to take it back.","Tap one above, then its match below.","Now tap its match.","Tap a step below to place it first.","WHY","WORD BY WORD","YOUR ORDER","Lesson complete","Every step counts \u2014 no matter how small.","The Path","For the one new to Islam \u2014 from the first word to daily practice","Welcome","The beginning","Welcome, and the shahada","You are welcome here","Saying the shahada \u2014 the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad \ufdfa is His Messenger \u2014 is the doorway into Islam. There is no ceremony required, no permission needed. Your intention, spoken honestly, is enough.","Take your time","This Path walks with you from your very first step \u2014 welcome, then purification, then your first prayer \u2014 at your pace. There are no timers and no tests that can fail you here.","Meet H\u0101di","H\u0101di is your guide inside Ar-Rayaan. Ask anything \u2014 every answer carries its source on screen.","Never despair","\u201cSay: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins.\u201d \u2014 Qur\u2019an 39:53","Purification","Preparing to stand before Allah","Wudu, step by step","Why we purify","Before standing in prayer, the Prophet \ufdfa taught us to wash in a specific way \u2014 wudu. Purity is half of faith, he said (Muslim 223). It is both a clean body and a quiet heart.","See the prayer times","Wudu is the doorway; prayer is the room beyond. Ar-Rayaan already keeps the day\u2019s prayer times for you \u2014 open them now to see when your next prayer arrives.","Order matters","Wudu has an order the Prophet \ufdfa taught: beginning with the intention, then washing the hands, rinsing the mouth and nose, washing the face, the arms to the elbows, wiping the head and ears, and finally the feet. Take it step by step, in this order.","A gentle check","What comes first in wudu?","The intention (niyyah)","Washing the feet","Wiping the head","Wudu begins with the intention in the heart, then the hands \u2014 remember the order: intention first.","In the taught order, the feet are washed\u2026","First, right after the intention","Last, after wiping the head and ears","Only if they look dirty","The feet come last in wudu, after wiping the head and ears \u2014 the order the Prophet \ufdfa taught.","Prayer I \u2014 The Body","Standing, bowing, prostrating","Your first prayer","The call to prayer","The adhan calls: Allahu Akbar \u2014 Allah is Greatest. You stand facing the qibla, intending prayer in your heart. The intention is in the heart \u2014 the Prophet \ufdfa said actions are by intentions (Bukhari 1). Then you raise your hands and say Allahu Akbar \u2014 the prayer has begun, and the world can wait.","The positions","Standing, you recite Al-Fatihah. Then bowing (rukoo\u02bf) with hands on knees, saying Subhana Rabbiy al-\u02bfAzeem. Then standing again, then prostration (sujood) \u2014 forehead, nose, palms, knees, toes on the ground \u2014 saying Subhana Rabbiy al-A\u02bfla. Sit, prostrate again: that is one rak\u02bfah. The Prophet \ufdfa said: pray as you have seen me pray (Bukhari 631).","Go slowly","Your first prayer may feel long. That is worship, not a performance. Ar-Rayaan keeps today\u2019s prayer times for you \u2014 open them, and when the next prayer arrives, walk through each position with this lesson beside you.","Prayer II \u2014 The Words","What you are saying to Allah","Al-Fatihah, word by word","Why Al-Fatihah matters","The Prophet \ufdfa said there is no prayer for the one who does not recite the Opening of the Book (Bukhari 756). Al-Fatihah is a conversation: Allah says He has divided the prayer between Himself and His servant, and each verse of Al-Fatihah is answered (Sahih Muslim 395). You praise, you ask, you worship.","Read it now, slowly","Open the reader and recite Al-Fatihah \u2014 one ayah at a time. Pause after each ayah and hold its meaning: praise \u2192 mercy \u2192 the Day \u2192 guidance.","A gentle check","Al-Fatihah begins with\u2026","Praise of Allah, Lord of the worlds","A list of rules","Stories of the prophets","Al-Fatihah opens with praise \u2014 \u201cAll praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds.\u201d Try reciting the first ayah once more.","Prayer III \u2014 The Life","Missed prayers, travel, Friday","Prayer in real life","Anchor to your day","Prayer is five appointments a day. Ar-Rayaan shows their times and the qibla direction \u2014 the app is built around them, because they are the skeleton of a Muslim\u2019s day.","When you miss one","Missed prayers are made up (qada) \u2014 the Gentle Ledger in My Journey helps you track them gently, one at a time. Never let shame stop you from returning; the door is always open.","Different schools, one prayer","Hands folded or at the sides, saying Ameen aloud or silently \u2014 the madhabs differ on details and agree on the prayer itself. Ar-Rayaan notes differences where they matter, exactly as it does with zakat. [Interpretive: madhab positions summarized; details sit with your local scholars.]","Fasting","The month and the voluntary days","How fasting works","The shape of a fast","From dawn (Fajr) to sunset (Maghrib): no food, no drink, no intimacy \u2014 and the Prophet \ufdfa added: no bad speech or action (Bukhari 1903). The body fasts; the tongue and heart fast too.","Begin with the voluntary","Outside Ramadan, the Prophet \ufdfa loved Mondays and Thursdays, and the White Days \u2014 the 13th, 14th, 15th of the lunar month (Tirmidhi 745, sahih per Darussalam; Abu Dawud 2449, sahih per al-Albani). The Ar-Rayaan calendar marks them for you \u2014 start there.","Zakat","Purification of wealth","Zakat, learned by doing","The third pillar","Zakat is a yearly giving of a small portion of saved wealth to eight categories of recipients (Qur\u2019an 9:60) \u2014 it purifies the rest. The word itself means purification and growth.","Compute a real example","Open the Guided Zakat Calculator and walk a full example through its seven sections \u2014 cash, gold, investments, debts. The calculator teaches nisab, hawl, and the madhab differences as you go.","Daily Life","Adhkar, food, the masjid","The rhythm of a Muslim day","Morning and evening adhkar","The Prophet \ufdfa taught words of protection and remembrance for morning and evening (Muslim 2723). The Dhikr & Du\u02bfa module carries them \u2014 begin with Ayat al-Kursi after Fajr.","Eating and gathering","Mention Allah\u2019s name before eating, eat with your right hand, and say the taught supplications after \u2014 small sunnahs that fill an ordinary day with light.","Beliefs","What a Muslim believes","The six articles of faith","The foundations","The Prophet \ufdfa defined faith in the hadith of Jibreel (Muslim 8): belief in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Last Day, and the divine decree. Everything else in the deen stands on these six.","Belief with the heart","Each article will grow with you for the rest of your life \u2014 faith deepens through worship and reflection, not through a single lesson. This is the beginning, not the test.","Character & Community","Living among people","The Muslim with family and strangers","When family does not understand","Many converts meet resistance at home. The Prophet \ufdfa was patient with those who opposed him, and the Qur'an asks a believer to keep good company with parents even when they disagree about faith (31:15) \u2014 kindness without compromise. If this weight feels heavy, the Sakina rooms are always open.","The best of you","The best of you are the best to their families (Tirmidhi 3895, hasan per Darussalam, sahih per al-Albani), and the most beloved to the Prophet \ufdfa are those best in character (Tirmidhi 2018, hasan per Darussalam). Start with one person, today.","Letters","Learn the letters and their sounds","Recitation","Tajweed, listening, and correction","Quranic Arabic","The words of the Qur\u2019an, one by one","Understanding","Word-by-word meanings and roots","This school is still being built, lesson by lesson. Lessons stay marked \u201cScholar review needed\u201d until a named scholar has reviewed them. The Path is ready for you today."],t.w)
